'''''4''''' is the second studio album by British rapper [[Aitch (rapper)|Aitch]], released on 20 June 2025. The album features guest appearances from Chimpo, Tigga Da Author, [[Pozer]], [[AJ Tracey]], [[Tamera Foster|Tamera]], [[Anne-Marie]], Kenzo Str8Drop and [[Avelino (rapper)|Avelino]]. The deluxe edition adds guest appearances from [[Nafe Smallz]] and [[Headie One]].<ref>{{cite web |title=4 Deluxe Download |url=https://aitch-gbp.myshopify.com/products/4-deluxe-download?fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAAac8tW0pNlyDGdkRj93ZQugllWsc2VnJ7eZt0ieE-BY9wxqTBLnjD6AJLXbMpg_aem_yEoeuTtr6xV5WKlKh9RZJA |website=Shopify |access-date=24 June 2025}}</ref> The album was released independently by Infinitum.<ref>{{cite web |title=Aitch – 4 |url=https://www.clashmusic.com/reviews/aitch-4/ |website=Clash Music |access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=HORVATH |first1=ZACHARY |title=Aitch Reps The "4" On His Sophomore Album |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/922659-aitch-4-stream |website=HotNewHipHop |access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Dana |first1=Danai |title=Culted Meets: Aitch got real with us for his new album drop |url=https://culted.com/culted-meets-aitch-new-album-4/ |website=Culted |access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref>

==Background==
On 17 April 2025, Aitch announced his second studio album, ''4'', through a pop-up event in [[Manchester]]. The rapper appeared at four locations across the city aboard a fire truck playing new music from the album.<ref>{{Cite news|last=Maidment|first=Adam|title=Aitch stuns fans in Manchester as he appears on top of fire truck for big announcement|url=https://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/whats-on/music-nightlife-news/aitch-stuns-fans-manchester-appears-31445403|date=17 April 2025|access-date=23 June 2025|newspaper=Manchester Evening}}</ref>

''4'' is a tribute to Aitch's roots, specifically referencing his Manchester postcode, M40, which inspired the album's title. He has stated that ''4'' is less personal than his debut album, ''[[Close to Home (Aitch album)|Close to Home]]'', and described it as more energetic, and representing the culture of Manchester.<ref>{{Cite magazine|last=Pilley|first=Max|title=Aitch announces second album '4': 'I'm just letting it all out'|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/aitch-announces-second-album-4-im-just-letting-it-all-out-3856103|date=18 April 2025|access-date=23 June 2025|magazine=[[NME]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine|first=Fred|last=Garratt-Stanley|url=https://www.rollingstone.co.uk/music/features/aitch-interview-photos-central-cee-new-album-51064/|title=Aitch: 'I just wanna set good examples and spread good vibes'|magazine=Rolling Stone|date=17 June 2025|access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref>

==Singles==
The lead single, "Straight Rhymez 2", a sequel to his breakout hit Straight Rhymez (2018), was released 6 March 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=Straight Rhymez 2 - Song by Aitch |url=https://music.apple.com/gb/song/straight-rhymez-2/1808036137 |website=Apple Music |access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref> The song charted at number 45 on the [[UK Independent Singles and Albums Charts|UK Independent Singles Chart]]. The second single "Bounce" was released on 19 March 2025.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Taylor |first1=Sam |title=Aitch has released a new independent single, 'Bounce' |url=https://readdork.com/news/aitch-returns-bounce-single/ |website=Dork |access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref> The third single "LUV?", featuring [[Anne-Marie]], was released on 24 April 2025. The single charted number 47 on the UK Independent Singles Chart.<ref>{{cite web |title=Aitch and Anne-Marie hook up again on new song LUV? |url=https://www.music-news.com/news/UK/181233/Aitch-and-Anne-Marie-hook-up-again-on-new-song-LUV |website=Music News |access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Stickler |first1=Jon |title=Aitch Unveils New Single LUV? Featuring Anne-Marie |url=https://www.stereoboard.com/content/view/247457/9 |website=Stereoboard |access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref> The fourth single "Till L4te", featuring [[Pozer]], was released on 22 May 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=Aitch enlists Pozer for new single 'TILL L4TE'|url=https://www.mixtapemadness.com/blog/music/aitch-enlists-pozer-for-new-single-till-l4te |website=Mixtape Madness |access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref> The fifth and final single "Col4 Body", featuring Tiggs Da Author, was released on 19 June.<ref name="UKchart">{{cite web|url=https://www.officialcharts.com/artist/54685/aitch/|title=AITCH – full Official Charts History|publisher=[[Official Charts Company]]|access-date=27 August 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190821194630/https://www.officialcharts.com/artist/54685/aitch/|archive-date=21 August 2019|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Critical reception==
{{Music ratings
| rev1 = ''[[Clash (magazine)|Clash]]'' 
| rev1score = 8/10<ref name=Clash>{{cite magazine|magazine=[[Clash (magazine)|Clash]]|last=Hill|first=Andy|title=Aitch 4. Blistering return to form from the Manc marvel|url=https://www.clashmusic.com/reviews/aitch-4/|date=19 June 2025|access-date=23 June 2025}}</ref>
}}

Andy Hill of ''[[Clash (magazine)|Clash]]'' described the album as a bold departure from the softer tone of his debut album, calling it a "treasure trove of bangers". However, he noted that its provocative lyrics, such as: "head so good / never doubt your intelligence", may divide listeners between seeing it as playful or [[misogyny|misogynistic]].<ref name="Clash"/>

