'''Bill Kahan Kapri'''<ref name=complex>{{cite web |url=https://www.complex.com/music/2020/03/kodak-black-pleads-guilty-gun-charge |title=Kodak Black Faces 2–7 Year Sentence After Pleading Guilty to Gun Charge |website=[[Complex Networks]] |date=March 12, 2020 |access-date=September 10, 2020 |archive-date=January 12, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210112233312/https://www.complex.com/music/2020/03/kodak-black-pleads-guilty-gun-charge |url-status=live}}</ref> (born '''Dieuson Octave'''; June 11, 1997), known professionally as '''Kodak Black''',<ref name="Macadams">{{cite web |last=Macadams |first=Torii |title=Born in the Trap: An Interview with Kodak Black |publisher=Passion of the Weiss |date=October 1, 2014 |url=http://www.passionweiss.com/2014/10/01/kodak-black-project-baby-interview/ |access-date=December 5, 2015 |archive-date=January 14, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210114080339/https://www.passionweiss.com/2014/10/01/kodak-black-project-baby-interview/ |url-status=live}}</ref> is an American rapper and singer-songwriter. Born and raised in [[Pompano Beach, Florida]], he gained initial recognition following the release of his 2014 songs "[[No Flockin]]" and "[[Skrt]]", both of which led him to sign a recording contract with [[Atlantic Records]]. The former received [[RIAA certification|double platinum]] certification by the [[Recording Industry of America]] (RIAA), while the latter received platinum certification; "No Flockin" marked his first entry on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] two years later as a [[sleeper hit]].<ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/artist/7409876/kodak-black/chart?f=379 |title=Chart History for Kodak Black (Billboard Hot 100) |magazine=Billboard |accessdate=March 30, 2024 |archive-date=October 5, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231005124309/https://www.billboard.com/artist/7409876/kodak-black/chart?f=379 |url-status=dead}}</ref> He also received local recognition around this time for a series of mixtapes he released between 2014 and 2016.

His 2017 single "[[Tunnel Vision (Kodak Black song)|Tunnel Vision]]" saw further commercial success, peaking at number six on the ''Billboard'' Hot 100. It preceded the release of his debut studio album ''[[Painting Pictures]]'' (2017), which peaked at number three on the [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]]. His debut commercial mixtape (and fifth overall), ''[[Project Baby 2]]'', was released that same year and peaked at number two on the chart, also spawning the [[RIAA certification|triple platinum]]-certified single "[[Roll in Peace]]" (featuring [[XXXTentacion]]). His second album, ''[[Dying to Live (Kodak Black album)|Dying to Live]]'' (2018), yielded his furthest commercial success and peaked atop the ''Billboard'' 200. It spawned the single "[[Zeze (song)|Zeze]]" (featuring [[Travis Scott]] and [[Offset (rapper)|Offset]]), which peaked at two on the ''Billboard'' Hot 100, received [[RIAA certification|sextuple platinum]] certification by the RIAA, and remains his highest-charting song. While incarcerated, he released his third album ''[[Bill Israel]]'' (2020), which was less commercially orientated. His 2021 single, "[[Super Gremlin]]", saw a commercial resurgence, peaking at number three on the ''Billboard'' Hot 100. It was included on fourth album, ''[[Back for Everything]]'' (2022). His fifth and sixth albums, ''[[Pistolz & Pearlz]]'' and ''[[When I Was Dead]]'', were both released in 2023, while his seventh album, ''[[Just Getting Started (Kodak Black album)|Just Getting Started]]'', was released in 2025 following a series of mixtapes.

Kodak Black's career has been marked by periods of mainstream success, as well as public controversies and legal issues. Although he remains as a largely successful artist and a high-profile figure within the hip-hop scene in Florida, his career has been marred by legal troubles that predate his musical career. Kodak Black was accused of [[rape]] in 2016 and faced the charge of [[Rape laws in the United States#South Carolina|first-degree criminal sexual conduct]] in [[South Carolina]]. He was given a [[plea bargain]] in 2021 to the lesser offense of [[assault]] and [[Battery (crime)|battery]] and was sentenced to [[probation]]. In 2019, he was arrested for [[making false statements]] to possess weapons and was sentenced to nearly four years in federal prison; his sentence was [[Commute a sentence|commuted]] by President [[Donald Trump]] in 2021. He was later arrested in May 2026 and arraigned in court on [[Illegal drug trade|drug trafficking]] charges.

== Early life ==
Kodak Black was born Dieuson Octave on June 11, 1997, to [[Haitians|Haitian]] immigrant Marcelene Octave in [[Pompano Beach, Florida]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.sun-sentinel.com/news/florida/fl-reg-kodak-black-profile-20170420-story.html |title=How Kodak Black made it big — and could lose it all |last=Clarkson |first=Brett |website=Sun-Sentinel |date=April 27, 2017 |access-date=November 13, 2019 |archive-date=February 4, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210204151217/https://www.sun-sentinel.com/news/florida/fl-reg-kodak-black-profile-20170420-story.html |url-status=live}}</ref> He was raised by his mother in Golden Acres, a [[Public housing in the United States|public housing project]] in Pompano Beach.<ref name="Macadams" /> Kodak Black is a known childhood friend of fellow Golden Acres native and professional football player [[Lamar Jackson]]; the two went to elementary school together and were close friends growing up.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.baltimoreravens.com/news/ravens-lamar-jackson-celebrate-with-rapper-kodak-black|title=Ravens, Lamar Jackson Celebrate With Rapper Kodak Black|work=Baltimore Ravens News|access-date=20 May 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://sports.yahoo.com/lamar-jackson-asks-donald-trump-to-pardon-imprisoned-rapper-kodak-black-235045027.html|title=Lamar Jackson asks President Trump to commute sentence of imprisoned rapper Kodak Black|work=Yahoo Sports|quote=Black and Jackson are childhood friends and attended the same elementary school in Florida.|access-date=20 May 2026}}</ref>

Kodak Black started rapping in elementary school and began to go to a local [[trap house]] after school to record music.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/41868-everything-you-need-to-know-about-kodak-black-news |title=Everything You Need To Know About Kodak Black |work=HotNewHipHop |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=February 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210202072714/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/everything-you-need-to-know-about-kodak-black-news.18400.html |url-status=live}}</ref> He spent his youth reading thesauruses and dictionaries to further his vocabulary.<ref>{{Cite news |url=http://www.sun-sentinel.com/news/florida/fl-reg-kodak-black-profile-20170420-story.html |title=How Kodak Black made it big — and could lose it all |last=Clarkson |first=Brett |work=Sun-Sentinel |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=February 4, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210204151217/https://www.sun-sentinel.com/news/florida/fl-reg-kodak-black-profile-20170420-story.html |url-status=live}}</ref> Kodak Black frequently participated in brawls and [[breaking and entering]] with his friends.<ref name="Macadams" /> He was expelled from school in the fifth grade for fighting and was arrested for auto theft while in middle school.<ref>{{Cite news |url=http://www.thefader.com/2016/01/28/kodak-black-gen-f-interview |title=Kodak Black Is America's Hardest Working Teenage Rapper |work=The FADER |access-date=November 1, 2017 |archive-date=November 8, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201108122346/http://www.thefader.com/2016/01/28/kodak-black-gen-f-interview |url-status=live}}</ref> About his upbringing, he said that he was given two options: "sell drugs with a gun on his hip or rap".<ref>{{Cite news |url=http://www.browardpalmbeach.com/music/kodak-black-talks-drake-co-sign-getting-locked-up-and-new-music-for-2016-7441039 |title=Kodak Black Talks Drake Co-Sign, Getting Locked Up, and New Music for 2016 |last=Jerome |first=Cristina |date=December 14, 2015 |work=New Times Broward-Palm Beach |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=February 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210202085238/https://www.browardpalmbeach.com/music/kodak-black-talks-drake-co-sign-getting-locked-up-and-new-music-for-2016-7441039 |url-status=live}}</ref>

From the age of six, Kodak Black used the nickname "Black". He also used the nickname "Lil' Black". When he joined [[Instagram]] he chose the username "Kodak Black", "...'cause you know [[Kodak]], that's pictures and all that." This later became his stage name when he started to rap and is the name favored by his fans.<ref name="Pigeons & Planes" /><ref name="Macadams" />

== Career ==

=== 2009–2015: Beginnings and ''Project Baby'' ===
In 2009, at age 12, Kodak Black joined a rap group called Brutal Youngnz, under the stage name J-Black.<ref name="J-Black" /> He then joined a local rap group called The Kolyons.<ref name="Macadams" /><ref name="KB-website">{{cite web |title=Biography |publisher=Kodak Black |url=http://kodak-world.com/?page_id=24 |url-status=dead |access-date=August 20, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170103124913/http://kodak-world.com/?page_id=24 |archive-date=January 3, 2017}}</ref> In December 2013, Kodak Black released his first [[mixtape]], ''Project Baby'',<ref>{{Citation |title=Project Baby by Kodak Black |date=December 26, 2013 |url=https://spinrilla.com/mixtapes/kodak-black-project-baby |access-date=July 14, 2016 |archive-date=September 30, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180930231834/https://spinrilla.com/mixtapes/kodak-black-project-baby |url-status=live}}</ref> followed in December 2014 with the mixtape ''Heart of the Projects'',<ref>{{Citation |title=Heart Of The Projects by Kodak Black |date=December 30, 2014 |url=https://spinrilla.com/mixtapes/kodak-black-heart-of-the-project |access-date=July 14, 2016 |archive-date=September 30, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180930231400/https://spinrilla.com/mixtapes/kodak-black-heart-of-the-project |url-status=live}}</ref> and in December 2015 with the mixtape ''Institution''.<ref>{{Citation |title=Institution by Kodak Black |date=December 25, 2015 |url=https://spinrilla.com/mixtapes/kodak-black-institution |access-date=July 14, 2016 |archive-date=October 1, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001030849/https://spinrilla.com/mixtapes/kodak-black-institution |url-status=live}}</ref>

In October 2015, Canadian rapper [[Drake (musician)|Drake]] posted a video of himself dancing to one of Kodak Black's songs, "[[Skrt]]", which helped him gain popularity<ref>{{cite web |last=Walker |first=Angus |title=Drake Dances To Kodak Black On Instagram |publisher=HotNewHipHop |date=October 24, 2015 |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/41375-drake-dances-to-kodak-black-on-instagram-news |access-date=December 5, 2015 |archive-date=July 9, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180709123404/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/drake-dances-to-kodak-black-on-instagram-news.18370.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://pigeonsandplanes.com/news/2016/03/kodak-black-drake |title=Kodak Black Reacts to the Drake Co-Sign: "You trying to show me you f**k with me or what?" |work=PigeonsandPlanes |access-date=August 16, 2016 |archive-date=August 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818154145/http://pigeonsandplanes.com/news/2016/03/kodak-black-drake |url-status=live}}</ref> despite objections from other rappers such as [[Earl Sweatshirt]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/41619-earl-sweatshirt-responds-to-drakes-kodak-black-cosign-news |title=Earl Sweatshirt Responds To Drake's Kodak Black Cosign |work=HotNewHipHop |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170818220258/http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/earl-sweatshirt-responds-to-drakes-kodak-black-cosign-news.18382.html |url-status=live}}</ref> That same month, he signed a deal with [[Atlantic Records]].<ref name="24h" /> In May 2016, Kodak Black and fellow American rapper [[Lil Uzi Vert]] announced their intention to partner for a national tour called the "Parental Advisory Tour"; however, Kodak Black did not appear on the tour.<ref>{{cite web |last=Low |first=Carver |title=Lil Uzi Vert & Kodak Black to Headline "Parental Advisory" Tour |publisher=Hotnewhiphop.com |date=May 6, 2016 |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/44719-lil-uzi-vert-and-kodak-black-to-headline-parental-advisory-tour-news |access-date=July 10, 2020 |archive-date=July 9, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180709123330/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/lil-uzi-vert-and-kodak-black-to-headline-parental-advisory-tour-news.21491.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== 2016–2017: Breakout, ''Painting Pictures'', and ''Project Baby 2'' ===
[[File:Kodak Black Press Photo by David Cabrera.jpg|thumb|upright|Kodak Black in 2016]]

In May 2016, he guest appeared on [[French Montana]]'s single "[[Lockjaw (song)|Lockjaw]]", which peaked at 23 on ''Billboard's'' [[Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Songs]] chart and was included on Montana's commercial mixtape ''[[MC4 (mixtape)|MC4]]''.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/artist/302488/french-montana/chart?f=367 |title=French Montana – Chart history {{!}} Billboard |magazine=Billboard |access-date=July 14, 2016 |archive-date=January 31, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170131070723/http://www.billboard.com/artist/302488/french-montana/chart?f=367 |url-status=live}}</ref> In August 2016, Kodak Black's single "Skrt" reached number 10 on ''Billboard's'' "Bubbling Under R&B/Hip-Hop Singles" chart.<ref name="Skrt">{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/biz/search/charts?f&#91;0&#93;=ts_chart_artistname%3Akodak%20black&f&#91;1&#93;=itm_field_chart_id%3A345&f&#91;2&#93;=ss_bb_type%3Achart_item&type=2&artist=kodak%20black |title=Kodak Black – Chart history (Bubbling Under R&B/Hip-Hop) |magazine=Billboard |access-date=October 26, 2016 |archive-date=February 11, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230211073922/https://www.billboard.com/c/music/ |url-status=live}}</ref> In June 2016, he released his fourth mixtape, ''Lil B.I.G. Pac'', which became his first mixtape to chart on ''Billboard'', reaching number 49 on the "Top R&B/Hip-Hop Albums" chart and number 18 on the [[Heatseekers Albums|Heatseakers Albums chart]].<ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/artist/7409876/kodak-black/chart |title=Kodak Black – Chart history {{!}} Billboard |magazine=Billboard |access-date=July 14, 2016 |archive-date=September 7, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170907201742/http://www.billboard.com/artist/7409876/kodak-black/chart |url-status=live}}</ref>

In June 2016, Kodak Black was named one of ''[[XXL (magazine)|XXL]]'' magazine's "2016 Freshman Class".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/xxl-freshman-class-of-2016-revealed-news.22200.html |title=XXL Freshman Class 2016 |last=Schwartz |first=Danny |date=June 19, 2016 |website=Hotnewhiphop |access-date=June 19, 2016 |archive-date=December 3, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181203104007/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/xxl-freshman-class-of-2016-revealed-news.22200.html |url-status=dead}}</ref>

In August 2016, Kodak Black was criticized when a studio session video was released showing him ridiculing dark-skinned black women with lyrics that implied those women were less attractive than light-skinned black women, which is considered a type of [[misogynoir]]—anti-Black hatred towards women.<ref>{{cite web |last=Cummings |first=Moriba |title=So Problematic: Kodak Black 'Doesn't Want No Black B***h' |publisher=BET |date=August 14, 2016 |url=https://www.bet.com/article/73fuvi/so-problematic-kodak-black-doesn-t-want-no-black-b-h |access-date=August 14, 2016 |archive-date=August 14, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160814160223/http://www.bet.com/music/2016/08/13/so-problematic--kodak-black--doesn-t-want-no-black-b---h-.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=DeCourcey |first=Danielle |title=What This Rapper Said About Black Women Reveals a Big Problem With Colorism |work=ATTN |date=August 12, 2016 |url=http://www.attn.com/stories/10664/twitter-reacts-colorism-kodak-black-lyrics |access-date=August 14, 2016 |archive-date=August 15, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160815082034/http://www.attn.com/stories/10664/twitter-reacts-colorism-kodak-black-lyrics |url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2016, Kodak Black released the song "Can I" while incarcerated.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/50630-hear-kodak-black-sing-a-beautiful-new-song-from-his-jail-cell-news |title=Kodak Black releases 'Can I' from Lil B.I.G. Pac |last=Walker |first=Angus |date=October 10, 2016 |website=Hotnewhiphop |access-date=October 10, 2016 |archive-date=October 11, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161011140441/http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/hear-kodak-black-sing-a-beautiful-new-song-from-his-jail-cell-news.24659.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

On February 17, 2017, Kodak Black released the single "[[Tunnel Vision (Kodak Black song)|Tunnel Vision]]".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://itunes.apple.com/us/album/tunnel-vision-single/id1204526233 |title=Tunnel Vision |publisher=iTunes Store}}{{dead link|date=March 2025|bot=medic}}{{cbignore|bot=medic}}</ref> The song debuted at number 27 and peaked at number 6, becoming Kodak Black's first top 10 hit on the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] and number 17 on the [[Canadian Hot 100]].<ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/artist/7409876/kodak-black/chart?f=379 |title=Kodak Black Chart History: Billboard Hot 100 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |access-date=March 14, 2017 |archive-date=May 15, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190515175552/https://www.billboard.com/artist/7409876/kodak-black/chart?f=379 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/artist/7409876/kodak-black/chart?f=793 |title=Kodak Black Chart History: Canadian Hot 100 |magazine=Billboard |access-date=March 14, 2017 |archive-date=May 15, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190515175611/https://www.billboard.com/artist/7409876/kodak-black/chart?f=793 |url-status=live}}</ref>

On March 31, 2017, Kodak Black released his debut [[studio album]] ''[[Painting Pictures]]''.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/03/stream-kodak-blacks-new-album-painting-pictures/ |title=Stream Kodak Black's New Album 'Painting Pictures' |website=XXL |date=March 31, 2017 |access-date=June 8, 2017 |archive-date=June 8, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170608120634/http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/03/stream-kodak-blacks-new-album-painting-pictures/ |url-status=live}}</ref> The album reached 3 on the [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]] and sold 71,000 equivalent units first week, a record for Kodak Black.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/04/kodak-black-painting-pictures-first-week-sales/ |title=Kodak Black's 'Painting Pictures' Album Enters Top 5 of Billboard 200 Chart |website=XXL |date=April 9, 2017 |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=August 26, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170826162120/http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/04/kodak-black-painting-pictures-first-week-sales/ |url-status=live}}</ref> While discussing rappers and fellow 2016 XXL Freshmen, [[Lil Uzi Vert]] and [[Lil Yachty]], Kodak Black created controversy when he insulted them whilst conducting a livestream on [[Instagram]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.vibe.com/2017/08/kodak-black-disses-lil-uzi-vert-and-lil-yachty/ |title=Kodak Black Isn't A Fan Of Lil Uzi Vert Or Lil Yachty |date=August 10, 2017 |work=Vibe |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170818220800/https://www.vibe.com/2017/08/kodak-black-disses-lil-uzi-vert-and-lil-yachty/ |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Lil Uzi Vert]] replied stating that he was not bothered by the insult and that he still "fucked with" Kodak Black.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.complex.com/music/2017/08/lil-uzi-vert-responds-kodak-black |title=Lil Uzi Vert Isn't Bothered by Kodak Black's Diss |website=Complex |date=August 14, 2017 |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170818221328/http://www.complex.com/music/2017/08/lil-uzi-vert-responds-kodak-black |url-status=live}}</ref> He released the follow-up to ''Project Baby'', ''Project Baby 2'', on August 18, 2017.<ref>{{Citation |title=Kodak Black – Project Baby 2 [Album Stream] {{!}} Stream [New Mixtape] |date=August 18, 2017 |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/454699-kodak-black-project-baby-2-album-stream-new-mixtape |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170818080224/http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kodak-black-project-baby-2-album-stream-new-mixtape.117441.html |url-status=live}}</ref> In November 2017, Kodak Black released a deluxe version of ''Project Baby 2'' titled ''Project Baby 2: All Grown Up''.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.xxlmag.com/rap-music/new-music/2017/11/kodak-black-releases-project-baby-2-all-grown-up-mixtape/ |title=Kodak Black Releases 'Project Baby 2: All Grown Up' Mixtape |website=XXL |date=November 24, 2017 |access-date=March 11, 2018 |archive-date=March 12, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180312022641/http://www.xxlmag.com/rap-music/new-music/2017/11/kodak-black-releases-project-baby-2-all-grown-up-mixtape/ |url-status=live}}</ref> The single from the deluxe version, "[[Codeine Dreaming]]", peaked at number 52 on the ''Billboard'' Hot 100.

=== 2018–2020: ''Heart Break Kodak'', ''Dying to Live'', and ''Bill Israel'' ===
[[File:Kodak Black October 2018.jpg|thumb|upright|Kodak Black in 2018]]

In January 2018, Kodak Black was arrested following a raid on his Florida home. Kodak Black later released the ''[[Heart Break Kodak]]'' mixtape on Valentine's Day.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://variety.com/2018/music/news/kodak-black-drops-valentines-day-mixtape-from-jail-1202698657/ |title=Kodak Black Drops Valentine's Day Mixtape — From Jail (Listen) |last=Aswad |first=Jem |date=February 14, 2018 |work=Variety |access-date=March 11, 2018 |archive-date=March 12, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180312083155/http://variety.com/2018/music/news/kodak-black-drops-valentines-day-mixtape-from-jail-1202698657/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kodak-black-new-project-heartbreak-kodak-valentines-day-8099480/ |title=Kodak Black Announces Anti-Valentine's Day Project 'Heartbreak Kodak' |magazine=Billboard |access-date=March 11, 2018 |archive-date=February 27, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180227221447/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/hip-hop/8099480/kodak-black-new-project-heartbreak-kodak-valentines-day |url-status=live}}</ref>

On December 14, 2018, Kodak Black released his second album ''[[Dying to Live (Kodak Black album)|Dying to Live]]''. The album was led by the successful single "[[Zeze (song)|Zeze]]" which featured rappers [[Travis Scott]] and [[Offset (rapper)|Offset]], as well as "[[If I'm Lyin, I'm Flyin]]", "Take One" and "[[Calling My Spirit]]". The album also featured rapper [[Lil Pump]] on "Gnarly", rapper [[Juice WRLD]] on "MoshPit", and paid tribute to deceased rapper [[XXXTentacion]].<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Saponara |first1=Michael |title=Kodak Black Releases 'Dying to Live' Album Feat. Lil Pump and Juice WRLD: Listen |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kodak-black-new-album-dying-to-live-stream-8490293/ |magazine=Billboard |date=December 14, 2018 |access-date=April 3, 2019 |archive-date=April 14, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414171248/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/hip-hop/8490293/kodak-black-new-album-dying-to-live-stream |url-status=live}}</ref> "Zeze" peaked at number 2 on the Hot 100, then "Calling My Spirit", also from the album, peaked at number 46. ''Dying to Live'' as a whole was on the ''Billboard'' 200 chart for 15 weeks, and peaked at number 1 for a week.<ref>{{cite magazine |title=Kodak Black |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/kodak-black/chart-history |magazine=Billboard |access-date=April 3, 2019 |archive-date=April 11, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190411025322/https://www.billboard.com/music/kodak-black/chart-history |url-status=live}}</ref>

On October 25, 2019, Kodak Black released "Zombie" with [[NLE Choppa]] and DB Omerta.<ref>{{cite web |title=Kodak Black Preps for Halloween With New Single 'Zombie' |url=https://hypebeast.com/2019/10/kodak-black-nle-choppa-db-omerta-zombie-stream |website=HypeBeast |date=October 25, 2019 |access-date=March 13, 2020 |archive-date=May 27, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200527220249/https://hypebeast.com/2019/10/kodak-black-nle-choppa-db-omerta-zombie-stream |url-status=live}}</ref> On February 14, 2020, Kodak Black released "Because of You", followed by a music video for the song.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Powell |first1=Jon |title=Kodak Black drops Valentine's Day single "Because Of You" |url=https://www.revolt.tv/2020/2/14/21138222/kodak-black-because-of-you |website=Revolt |date=February 14, 2020 |access-date=March 13, 2020 |archive-date=March 4, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200304061717/https://www.revolt.tv/2020/2/14/21138222/kodak-black-because-of-you |url-status=live}}</ref> Kodak Black then claimed that if the song was [[Music recording certification#RIAA certification|certified platinum]] by his birthday, then he would release an album.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Coleman II |first1=Vernon |title=Kodak Black Says He'll Wait Until He's Released From Prison to Drop Album If New Single Doesn't Go Platinum by His Birthday |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2020/02/kodak-black-wait-until-released-from-prison-new-album/ |website=XXL |date=February 16, 2020 |publisher=XXL Magazine |access-date=March 13, 2020 |archive-date=March 13, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200313031243/https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2020/02/kodak-black-wait-until-released-from-prison-new-album/ |url-status=live}}</ref> On May 12, 2020, he released the single "Vultures Cry 2", featuring WizDaWizard and Mike Smiff.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://music.apple.com/us/album/vultures-cry-2-feat-wizdawizard-and-mike-smiff-single/1517448013 |title=VULTURES CRY 2 (feat. WizDaWizard and Mike Smiff) – Single by Kodak Black on Apple Music |date=June 11, 2020 |via=[[Apple Music]] |access-date=June 18, 2020 |archive-date=December 17, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201217052603/https://music.apple.com/us/album/vultures-cry-2-feat-wizdawizard-and-mike-smiff-single/1517448013 |url-status=live}}</ref>

On November 11, 2020, Kodak returned with his third album, ''[[Bill Israel]]'', while serving a prison sentence.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/332925-kodak-black-changes-new-album-title-shares-cover-artwork-news |title=Kodak Black Changes New Album Title, Shares Cover Artwork |work=HotNewHipHop |last=Zidel |first=Alex |date=October 26, 2020 |accessdate=February 6, 2021 |archive-date=November 13, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201113063537/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kodak-black-changes-new-album-title-shares-cover-artwork-news.120270.html?_amp |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== 2020–present: Prison release, ''Haitian Boy Kodak'', ''Back for Everything'' and ''Kutthroat Bill: Vol. 1'' ===

On January 23, 2021, he released the single, "[[Last Day In]]", in which he addresses his release from prison due to his pardon from President Donald Trump.<ref>{{cite web |last=Yoo |first=Noah |date=January 23, 2020 |title=Kodak Black Addresses Clemency on New Song 'Last Day In' |url=https://www.pitchfork.com/news/kodak-black-addresses-clemency-on-new-song-last-day-in |work=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]] |accessdate=February 6, 2021 |archive-date=January 26, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210126114414/https://pitchfork.com/news/kodak-black-addresses-clemency-on-new-song-last-day-in/ |url-status=live}}</ref> He released the single, "Every Balmain", on February 6, 2021, in which he discusses life post-prison.<ref>{{cite web |last=Will |first=Richards |date=February 6, 2021 |title=Kodak Black discusses his post-prison lifestyle on new song 'Every Balmain' |url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/kodak-black-discusses-his-post-prison-lifestyle-on-new-song-every-balmain-2874269 |work=[[NME]] |accessdate=February 6, 2021 |archive-date=February 6, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210206142251/https://www.nme.com/news/music/kodak-black-discusses-his-post-prison-lifestyle-on-new-song-every-balmain-2874269 |url-status=live}}</ref>
On February 19, he was featured on [[Lil Yachty]]'s single, "[[Hit Bout It]]", which was released alongside a music video.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Althea |first=Legaspi |date=February 19, 2021 |title=Lil Yachty, Kodak Black Team Up for New 'Hit Bout It' Video |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/lil-yachty-kodak-black-hit-bout-it-video-1130250 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]] |accessdate=February 20, 2021 |archive-date=October 20, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221020000909/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/lil-yachty-kodak-black-hit-bout-it-video-1130250/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Kodak released a mixtape titled ''Haitian Boy Kodak'' on May 14, 2021. The project's cover art pays tribute to his Haitian pride.<ref>{{cite web |last=Saponara |first=Michael |date=May 1, 2021 |title=Kodak Black Readies New Album To Match Up With J. Cole |url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.62055/title.kodak-black-haitian-boy-kodak-album-to-face-off-against-j-cole-this-friday |accessdate=May 1, 2021 |work=[[HipHopDX]] |archive-date=May 11, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210511203047/https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.62055/title.kodak-black-haitian-boy-kodak-album-to-face-off-against-j-cole-this-friday |url-status=live}}</ref> Kodak voiced frustration at the mixtape only moving 22,000 units in its first week, claiming that listeners had turned their backs on [[gangsta rap]].<ref name="Birthday">{{cite web |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/360517-kodak-black-announces-happy-birthday-kodak-release-date-news |title=Kodak Black Announces 'Happy Birthday Kodak' Release Date |work=HotNewHipHop |last=Findlay |first=Mitch |date=May 24, 2021 |access-date=May 25, 2021 |archive-date=February 11, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230211073930/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/360517-kodak-black-announces-happy-birthday-kodak-release-date-news |url-status=live}}</ref> Kodak released his next project, ''Happy Birthday Kodak'', on June 11, 2021, his twenty-fourth birthday.<ref name="Birthday" /> On November 1, 2021, Kodak released a music video for the song "[[Super Gremlin]]", from Syko Bob and Snapkatt's Halloween-themed mixtape, ''Sniper Gang Presents Syko Bob & Snapkatt: Nightmare Babies'', an 11-track project, of which Kodak appears on eight tracks.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.revolt.tv/platform/new-music/2021/11/2/22759255/kodak-black-super-gremlin-video |title=Kodak Black becomes a 'Super Gremlin' in new visual |work=[[Revolt (TV network)|Revolt]] |last=Powell |first=Jon |date=November 1, 2021 |access-date=November 9, 2021}}{{Dead link|date=February 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> "Super Gremlin" became a hit, peaking at number five on the ''Billboard'' Hot 100.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Atkinson |first=Katie |date=January 27, 2022 |title=Here Are the Lyrics to Kodak Black's 'Super Gremlin' |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/lyrics/kodak-black-super-gremlin-lyrics-1235023667/ |access-date=February 27, 2022 |magazine=Billboard |archive-date=February 27, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220227052845/https://www.billboard.com/music/lyrics/kodak-black-super-gremlin-lyrics-1235023667/ |url-status=live}}</ref> The song was also included on Kodak's fourth studio album ''[[Back for Everything]]'', which released on February 25, 2022.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Listen to Kodak Black's New Project 'Back for Everything' f/ Lil Durk |url=https://www.complex.com/music/kodak-black-back-for-everything-stream |access-date=February 27, 2022 |website=Complex |date=February 25, 2022 |archive-date=February 27, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220227082006/https://www.complex.com/music/kodak-black-back-for-everything-stream |url-status=live}}</ref> The project proceeded to peak at number 2 on the ''Billboard 200''.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/encanto-billboard-200-chart-number-one-eighth-week-1235040129/ |title='Encanto' Enchants Billboard 200 Albums Chart With Eighth Week at No. 1 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |author=Keith Caulfield |date=March 6, 2022 |accessdate=February 2, 2023 |archive-date=March 6, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220306213543/https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/encanto-billboard-200-chart-number-one-eighth-week-1235040129/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Months later, following the release of his viral singles "[[Walk/Spin]]", Kodak announced his departure from Atlantic Records and that he would sign to [[Capitol Records]] for an eight-figure record deal.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/kodak-black-headed-capitol-records-after-finishes-atlantic-deal/ |title=Kodak Black Is Headed to Capitol — He Just Has to Release Some More Records With Atlantic First |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |author=Elias Leight |date=October 25, 2022 |accessdate=February 2, 2023 |archive-date=February 2, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230202213912/https://www.billboard.com/pro/kodak-black-headed-capitol-records-after-finishes-atlantic-deal/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Kodak's final project with Atlantic, ''Kutthroat Bill: Vol. 1'' was released on October 28, 2022.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Kodak Black Releases New Album 'Kutthroat Bill: Vol. 1' |url=https://www.complex.com/music/kodak-black-kutthroat-bill-vol-1 |access-date=October 28, 2022 |website=Complex |date=October 28, 2022 |archive-date=October 28, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221028041046/https://www.complex.com/music/kodak-black-kutthroat-bill-vol-1 |url-status=live}}</ref> The mixtape proceeded to peak at number 8 on the ''Billboard 200''.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/taylor-swift-midnights-number-one-billboard-200-2nd-week-1235167312/ |title=Taylor Swift's 'Midnights' Spends Second Week at No. 1 on Billboard 200 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |author=Keith Caulfield |date=November 7, 2022 |accessdate=February 2, 2023 |archive-date=November 16, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221116094937/https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/taylor-swift-midnights-number-one-billboard-200-2nd-week-1235167312/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Kodak Black collaborated with [[Kendrick Lamar]] on "[[Silent Hill (song)|Silent Hill]]" from the latter's double album, ''[[Mr. Morale & the Big Steppers]]'' (2022). Due to Kodak Black's conviction involving the 2016 sexual assault case which was reduced to first-degree assault, both performers generated greater controversy.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Writer |first=Ashley Gale Off-Platform Staff |date=May 13, 2022 |title=Kendrick Lamar Fans Call Out Rapper After Featuring Kodak Black on Album |url=https://www.newsweek.com/kendrick-lamar-fans-call-out-rapper-after-featuring-kodak-black-album-1706598 |access-date=October 29, 2023 |website=Newsweek |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Fitzgerald |first=Trent |date=May 14, 2022 |title=Kendrick Lamar Faces Backlash for Featuring Kodak Black on New Album Mr. Morale & The Big Steppers |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/kendrick-lamar-backlash-kodak-black-morale-big-steppers/ |access-date=October 29, 2023 |website=XXL Mag |language=en}}</ref>

== Musical style ==

Kodak Black's music is frequently about "previous and future criminal misdeeds", and he stated that he has been influenced by rappers [[Boosie Badazz]] and [[Chief Keef]].<ref name="Macadams" />

A writer for ''[[The New Yorker]]'' magazine described his "manifestly youthful voice" and "mutinous sound", and stated "Kapri joins other young rappers who have rejected an old-school emphasis on lyrical variety, individualism, and personal catharsis".<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Trammell |first=Matthew |title=Teenage Dream |magazine=The New Yorker |date=April 25, 2016 |url=http://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2016/04/25/the-teenagers-shaping-pop |access-date=June 13, 2016 |archive-date=October 1, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001031101/https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2016/04/25/the-teenagers-shaping-pop |url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2016, a music critic wrote in ''[[The Fader]]'' that Kodak Black "articulates the constant state of affliction that living in a poverty-stricken environment can mean. He makes emotionally intelligent observations in a manner reminiscent of teenage artists of the '90s, such as [[Mobb Deep]] and [[Lil Wayne]], whose voices were valued as genuine illustrations of life in their corners of America."<ref>{{cite web |last=Burney |first=Lawrence |title=Why Kodak Black's American Story Is So Important |publisher=The Fader |date=July 20, 2016 |url=http://www.thefader.com/2016/07/20/kodak-black-lil-big-pac-essay |access-date=July 29, 2016 |archive-date=September 30, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180930231603/http://www.thefader.com/2016/07/20/kodak-black-lil-big-pac-essay |url-status=live}}</ref>

Kodak Black has been frequently described as a [[mumble rap]]per.<ref>{{cite news |title=Declaring a Moratorium on the Term 'Mumble Rap' |url=https://www.theringer.com/2017/4/18/16047136/mumble-rap-moratorium-lil-yachty-desiigner-15bc3647dae9 |first=Justin |last=Charity |newspaper=The Ringer |date=April 18, 2017 |access-date=October 11, 2018 |archive-date=December 25, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171225092014/https://www.theringer.com/2017/4/18/16047136/mumble-rap-moratorium-lil-yachty-desiigner-15bc3647dae9 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Kodak Black mumbles freestyle for 12 minutes (MUMBLE RAP EXCELLENCE) |date=December 24, 2017 |url=https://www.kanyetothe.com/forum/index.php?topic=7300426.0 |access-date=October 11, 2018 |archive-date=October 12, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181012053915/https://www.kanyetothe.com/forum/index.php?topic=7300426.0 |url-status=live}}</ref>

== Personal life ==

In 2014, Kodak Black stated that he was working towards his high school diploma at [[Blanche Ely High School]] in Pompano Beach.<ref name="Macadams" /><ref name="Ivey" />

During his incarceration, Kodak Black began to identify as a [[Black Hebrew Israelites|Hebrew Israelite]] after a priest who conducts prison ministry studied scripture with him.<ref>{{Cite news |url=http://forward.com/fast-forward/374727/first-kendrick-lamar-now-kodak-black-another-rapper-goes-hebrew-israelite/ |title=Rapper Kodak Black Goes Hebrew Israelite |work=The Forward |access-date=August 9, 2017 |archive-date=November 12, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201112021417/http://forward.com/fast-forward/374727/first-kendrick-lamar-now-kodak-black-another-rapper-goes-hebrew-israelite/ |url-status=live}}</ref> He later filed to change his name to Bill Kahan Blanco, with Kahan supposedly being an alternative spelling of [[kohen]], a term used in [[Judaism]] to refer to priests who descend from the prophet [[Aaron]], the brother of [[Moses]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=http://forward.com/fast-forward/376794/rap-star-kodak-black-wants-a-hebrew-name-the-one-priests-have/ |title=Rap Star Kodak Black Wants To Give Himself The Name Of A Biblical Priest |work=The Forward |access-date=August 9, 2017 |archive-date=February 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210202215209/https://forward.com/fast-forward/376794/rap-star-kodak-black-wants-a-hebrew-name-the-one-priests-have/ |url-status=live}}</ref> On May 2, 2018, he legally changed his name from "Dieuson Octave" to "Bill Kahan Kapri".<ref name=complex/>

In June 2017, he wrote on Instagram about his preference for light-skinned women over those with dark skin. He also stated in an interview that actress [[Keke Palmer]] was "straight", but that he "don't really like Black girls like that".<ref>{{Cite news |url=http://www.essence.com/celebrity/kodak-black-black-women-comments |title=Kodak Black Is Standing By His Brash Comments About Dark-Skinned Black Women |date=June 29, 2017 |work=Essence |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170818221820/http://www.essence.com/celebrity/kodak-black-black-women-comments |url-status=live}}</ref> Some Twitter users responded negatively,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.complex.com/music/2017/06/kodak-black-says-he-doesnt-like-black-girls |title=Kodak Black: 'I Don't Really Like Black Girls Like That' |website=Complex |date=June 25, 2017 |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170818221004/http://www.complex.com/music/2017/06/kodak-black-says-he-doesnt-like-black-girls |url-status=live}}</ref> provoking Kodak Black to delete both his Instagram and Twitter accounts.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/06/kodak-black-deletes-instagram-controversial-comments-black-women/ |title=Kodak Black Deletes Instagram Account After Controversy Over Comments on Black Women |last=India |first=Lindsey |date=June 27, 2017 |work=XXL |access-date=July 22, 2017 |archive-date=July 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170718125654/http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/06/kodak-black-deletes-instagram-controversial-comments-black-women/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Kodak Black also stated that light-skinned women are easier to break down, black women are "too gutter", and that he does not like his skin complexion.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/newsbeat-40479291 |title=Kodak Black says light-skinned women are easier to break down – BBC Newsbeat |date=March 7, 2017 |website=BBC Newsbeat |access-date=August 18, 2017 |archive-date=August 8, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170808194141/http://www.bbc.co.uk/newsbeat/article/40479291/kodak-black-says-light-skinned-women-are-easier-to-break-down |url-status=live}}</ref>

In June 2018, Kodak Black earned his [[GED]] while in prison.<ref>{{cite news |date=July 2, 2018 |title='Momma I Know I'm Late But I Got It'- Kodak Black Passes GED Test in Prison |url=https://olisa.tv/celebrity/momma-i-know-im-late-but-i-got-it-kodak-black-passes-ged-test-in-prison/ |work=Olisa.tv |access-date=August 7, 2018 |archive-date=August 8, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180808011847/https://olisa.tv/celebrity/momma-i-know-im-late-but-i-got-it-kodak-black-passes-ged-test-in-prison/ |url-status=dead}}</ref>

On February 6, 2021, Kodak returned to social media with a new hairstyle and a slimmer figure.<ref name="NewLook">{{cite web |url=https://www.complex.com/music/kodak-black-resurfaces-new-look-following-trump-pardon |title=Kodak Black Resurfaces Following Trump Pardon With New Look |work=[[Complex (magazine)|Complex]] |last=Price |first=Joe |date=February 5, 2021 |accessdate=February 6, 2021 |archive-date=February 5, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210205175629/https://www.complex.com/music/kodak-black-resurfaces-new-look-following-trump-pardon |url-status=live}}</ref> The same day, he posted a video to Twitter where he and his lawyer [[Bradford Cohen]] said that they had informed the FBI in Miami that Kodak would cover tuition costs for the two children of late FBI agent Laura Schwartzenberger and the child of late FBI agent Daniel Alfin, both of whom [[2021 Sunrise, Florida shootout|died on duty]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.revolt.tv/article/2021-02-06/60372/kodak-black-offers-to-pay-tuition-for-children-of-two-slain-fbi-agents/ |title=Kodak Black offers to pay tuition for children of two slain FBI agents |work=[[Revolt (TV network)|Revolt]] |date=February 6, 2021 |access-date=June 21, 2023}}</ref>

On February 12, 2022, Kodak Black was shot during a fight outside a [[Los Angeles]] Italian restaurant where [[Justin Bieber]] was hosting a [[Super Bowl LVI|Super Bowl]]-week party.<ref>{{cite web |first=Christopher |last=Cann |agency=Associated Press |title=Rapper Kodak Black reportedly among 4 shot outside Super Bowl party in California |url=https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/2022/02/15/3-people-and-kodak-black-shot-los-angeles-super-bowl-party/6795686001/ |access-date=February 21, 2022 |website=Tallahassee Democrat |language=en-US |archive-date=May 22, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220522164638/https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/2022/02/15/3-people-and-kodak-black-shot-los-angeles-super-bowl-party/6795686001/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Kapri endorsed the [[Donald Trump 2024 presidential campaign]], releasing the single "ONBOA47RD" with New York rapper [[Fivio Foreign]] in support of Trump.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Gee |first=Andre |date=August 16, 2024 |title=Fivio Foreign and Kodak Black's Embarrassing Trump-Endorsement Track |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/fivio-foreign-trump-endorsement-why-1235081799/ |access-date=September 14, 2024 |magazine=Rolling Stone |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Vassolo |first=Martin |date=August 16, 2024 |title=Florida rapper Kodak Black releases Trump campaign song |url=https://www.axios.com/local/miami/2024/08/16/donald-trump-kodak-black-campaign-song-onboa47rd |access-date=September 14, 2024 |work=[[Axios (website)|Axios]]}}</ref>

=== Philanthropy ===

On October 1, 2018, Kodak Black donated $10,000 to the Jack and Jill Children's center, which is a provider of early children's education.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Post |first1=Chantilly |title=Kodak Black Donates Over $10K For Early Childhood Education |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/122402-kodak-black-donates-over-s10k-for-early-childhood-education-news |website=hotnewhiphop |date=October 2018 |publisher=Hot New Hip Hop |access-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-date=November 11, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201111214445/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kodak-black-donates-over-s10k-for-early-childhood-education-news.61099.html |url-status=live}}</ref> In November 2018, Kodak Black announced that he was building a school in [[Haiti]].<ref>{{cite web |author=Tania |title=Kodak Black Announces Plans To Build A School In Haiti |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/132782-kodak-black-announces-plans-to-build-a-school-in-haiti-news |website=hotnewhiphop |date=November 5, 2018 |publisher=Hot New Hip Hop |access-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-date=October 13, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191013131126/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kodak-black-announces-plans-to-build-a-school-in-haiti-news.63793.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

On December 20, 2018, Kodak Black donated enough money to Paradise Childcare in Broward County, Florida, to provide gifts for 150 children in the area. In addition, he also donated $5,000 for the organization's annual Christmas party.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Cole |first1=Alexander |title=Kodak Black Channels Santa Claus With Generous Christmas Donation |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/169286-kodak-black-channels-santa-claus-with-generous-christmas-donation-news |website=hotnewhiphop |date=December 20, 2018 |publisher=Hot New Hip Hop |access-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-date=February 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210202220236/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kodak-black-channels-santa-claus-with-generous-christmas-donation-news.67332.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

In late 2018, he donated $2,500 to the family of South Carolina police officer Terrence Carraway, who was killed in a shootout on duty. On May 3, 2019, Kodak Black donated $12,500 to Paige Cook, to help with the girl's goal to give pencils and notebooks to all 7,600 students in the Cleburne Independent School District in Texas, a low-income district. In 2018, Paige raised enough money to buy over 40,000 pencils.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Marie |first1=Erika |title=Kodak Black Donates Over $12K To Help Low-Income Students: Report |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/175048-kodak-black-donates-over-s12k-to-help-low-income-students-report-news |website=hotnewhiphop |date=May 3, 2019 |publisher=Hot New Hip Hop |access-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-date=February 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210202121541/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kodak-black-donates-over-s12k-to-help-low-income-students-report-news.79044.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Centeno |first1=Tony |title=KODAK BLACK DONATES OVER $12,000 TO LOW-INCOME STUDENTS: REPORT |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/05/kodak-black-money-student-donation/ |website=xxlmag.com |date=May 3, 2019 |publisher=XXL Magazine |access-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-date=April 24, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200424164729/https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/05/kodak-black-money-student-donation/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

In the wake of the [[2019 STEM School Highlands Ranch shooting]], Kodak Black's lawyer reached out to the family of Kendrick Ray Castillo, who was shot and killed after lunging at the attacker, on May 11, and offered to pay for Castillo's funeral and set aside an annual $10,000 scholarship for any student wishing to go to college for science or engineering. His lawyer stated that the family had not yet responded.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Coleman |first1=Vernon |title=KODAK BLACK OFFERS TO PAY FOR FUNERAL OF SLAIN COLORADO TEEN |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/05/kodak-black-funeral-colorado-teen/ |newspaper=XXL Mag |publisher=XXL Magazine |access-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-date=May 13, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190513160818/https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/05/kodak-black-funeral-colorado-teen/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Kodak also allegedly donated $50,000 to Gekyume, the son of late rapper and collaborator [[XXXTentacion]]. Kodak and XXXTentacion were friends up until [[killing of XXXTentacion|his death in 2018]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Berry |first1=Peter |title=DJ Scheme says Kodak Black sent XXXTentacion's song $50,000 |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/06/kodak-black-xxxtentacion-son-gekyume-money/ |website=XXL |date=June 19, 2019 |access-date=February 6, 2020 |archive-date=February 6, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200206144939/https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/06/kodak-black-xxxtentacion-son-gekyume-money/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

In July 2025, Kodak was awarded a [[Freedom of the City#Key to the city|key to the city]] of Pompano Beach, Florida, his hometown.<ref>[https://www.miamiherald.com/miami-com/miami-com-news/article310386260.html Kodak Black just got a key to his hometown. Not everyone is congratulating him]</ref>

== Legal issues ==

=== 2015–2017 ===

[[File:Kodak Black, arrest photo, May 2016.png|thumb|upright|Kodak Black's mugshot in May 2016]]

Kodak Black was placed into a [[youth detention center]] three times in one year, and then placed on probation.<ref name="KB-website" />

In October 2015, he was arrested in Pompano Beach and charged with robbery, battery, false imprisonment of a child, and possession of [[cannabis]]. He was later released.<ref name="Local 10" /> He was later arrested once again on December 25, 2015 in [[St. Lucie County, Florida|St. Lucie County]] on charges relating to drugs.<ref name=LegalHistory/>

In April 2016, Kodak Black was arrested in [[Hallandale Beach, Florida]], and charged with possession of a weapon by a convicted felon, possession of marijuana, and fleeing from officers.<ref>{{cite web |title=South Florida Rapper 'Kodak Black' Arrested in Hallandale Beach |work=WSVN-TV |date=April 22, 2016 |url=http://wsvn.com/news/local/south-florida-rapper-arrested-in-hallandale-beach/ |access-date=June 13, 2016 |archive-date=June 25, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160625080350/http://wsvn.com/news/local/south-florida-rapper-arrested-in-hallandale-beach/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

The following month in May 2016, he was arrested in [[Broward County, Florida]], and charged with armed robbery and false imprisonment. He was detained in custody.<ref name="Ivey">{{cite web |url=http://www.xxlmag.com/rap-music/new-music/2016/05/kodak-black-jewels/ |title=Kodak Black Drops "Jewels" |last=Ivey |first=Justin |date=May 24, 2016 |work=XXL |access-date=June 13, 2016 |archive-date=December 17, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191217180925/https://www.xxlmag.com/rap-music/new-music/2016/05/kodak-black-jewels/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Rapper 'Kodak Black' Arrested Again in South Florida |work=WSVN-TV |date=May 19, 2016 |url=http://wsvn.com/news/local/south-florida-rapper-arrested-second-time-this-year/ |access-date=June 13, 2016 |archive-date=June 22, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160622080739/http://wsvn.com/news/local/south-florida-rapper-arrested-second-time-this-year/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

In August 2016, he appeared in court in [[Fort Lauderdale]], [[Florida]]. Several executives from Atlantic Records attended the court; vice-president Michael Kushner commented "Black has a bright future as a recording artist".<ref name="Clarkson">{{cite web |last1=Clarkson |first1=Brett |last2=Anthony |first2=Attiyya |title=Kodak Black Staying in Jail After Authorities Discover Outstanding Warrants |work=Sun Sentinel |date=August 17, 2016 |url=http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-kodak-black-still-in-jail-20160817-story.html |access-date=August 20, 2016 |archive-date=September 30, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180930231424/http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-kodak-black-still-in-jail-20160817-story.html |url-status=live}}</ref> Kodak Black pleaded [[no contest]] to all charges and under a plea agreement was to be placed on house arrest for one year, have five years' probation, perform community service as required, and take anger management classes. He would also be permitted to tour internationally.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/51165-kodak-black-to-be-released-on-house-arrest-news |title=Kodak Black To Be Released On House Arrest |website=HNHH |date=August 16, 2016 |access-date=August 16, 2016 |archive-date=October 1, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001070410/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kodak-black-to-be-released-on-house-arrest-news.23511.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-kodak-black-court-appearance-20160816-story.html |title=Kodak Black to be released; Pompano Beach rapper gets house arrest, probation |first=South Florida |last=Sun-Sentinel |access-date=August 16, 2016 |archive-date=August 17, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160817190004/http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-kodak-black-court-appearance-20160816-story.html |url-status=live}}</ref> Before his release from Broward Main Jail, police discovered two outstanding criminal warrants, the first from [[Florence, South Carolina]] alleging felony criminal sexual conduct, the second from [[St. Lucie County, Florida]] alleging two counts of misdemeanor marijuana possession. Kodak Black was not released from jail.<ref name="Clarkson" />

In September 2016, Kodak Black pleaded no contest to two misdemeanor drug charges and was sentenced to four months in jail. He was credited for time spent in custody awaiting trial and was required to serve 120 days. He was also suspended from driving for one year.<ref>{{cite web |last=Clarkson |first=Brett |title=Kodak Black Gets 120 Days In Jail, License Suspended For A Year In St. Lucie County Case |work=[[Sun-Sentinel]] |date=September 19, 2016 |url=http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-kodak-black-fort-pierce-court-20160906-story.html |access-date=October 7, 2016 |archive-date=September 21, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160921201857/http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-kodak-black-fort-pierce-court-20160906-story.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

Kodak Black was released from jail in Florida and was then transported to [[Florence, South Carolina]], to face charges of sexual assault. According to the victim, who reported the incident to her school nurse, she had attended a February 2016 performance by Kodak Black at "Treasure City" in Florence, after which she accompanied him to his hotel room where he is alleged to have told her he "couldn't help himself" as he tore off her clothes, bit her repeatedly, and raped her as she screamed for help. Kodak Black was released from custody in South Carolina on December 1, 2016, after posting a $100,000 bond, but returned to court on February 8, 2017.<ref>{{cite web |last=Clarkson |first=Brett |title=Kodak Black Released From Jail On $100K Bond |work=Sun Sentinel |date=December 1, 2016 |url=http://www.sun-sentinel.com/news/florida/fl-kodak-black-south-carolina-incident-report-20161201-story.html |access-date=December 25, 2016 |archive-date=September 30, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180930231713/http://www.sun-sentinel.com/news/florida/fl-kodak-black-south-carolina-incident-report-20161201-story.html |url-status=live}}</ref> About Kodak Black, the ''[[Miami New Times]]'' asked: "is he the product of larger societal problems, having been raised on a steady diet of misogynistic rap lyrics?"<ref>{{cite web |last=Farzan |first=Antonia |title=Kodak Black, Accused of Sexual Assault, Still Reaches for the Top |work=Miami New Times |date=January 17, 2017 |url=http://www.miaminewtimes.com/music/kodak-black-accused-of-sexual-assault-still-reaches-for-the-top-9068685 |access-date=January 18, 2017 |archive-date=January 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170118145017/http://www.miaminewtimes.com/music/kodak-black-accused-of-sexual-assault-still-reaches-for-the-top-9068685 |url-status=live}}</ref> Within hours of release, he recorded and released "[[There He Go]]",<ref>{{cite web |last=Weinstein |first=Max |title=Kodak Black Releases First New Song and Video Since Getting Out of Jail |work=XXL |date=December 6, 2016 |url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2016/12/kodak-black-there-he-go-video/ |access-date=December 25, 2016 |archive-date=December 26, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161226060931/http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2016/12/kodak-black-there-he-go-video/ |url-status=live}}</ref> a single which mentions his recent release from jail:
<blockquote><poem>Just hopped off the plane I just got out about a day ago
Everybody love me, when they see me they be like, "There he go!"
Got me a new lady, we 'bout to take a trip to Mexico
Crackers took my .40 so I'm 'bout to go buy a Draco<ref>{{cite web |last=Kodak Black |title=There He Go |work=Urban Islandz |date=December 8, 2016 |url=http://urbanislandz.com/2016/12/08/kodak-black-there-he-go-lyrics/ |access-date=December 25, 2016 |archive-date=September 21, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180921190934/https://urbanislandz.com/2016/12/08/kodak-black-there-he-go-lyrics/ |url-status=live}}</ref></poem></blockquote>

In February 2017, Kodak Black was arrested again for violation of his probation. He was held without bond and his musical tour was postponed.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/02/kodak-black-arrested-probation-violation/ |title=Kodak Black Arrested for Probation Violation – XXL |website=XXL Mag |date=February 28, 2017 |access-date=March 1, 2017 |archive-date=March 1, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170301020813/http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2017/02/kodak-black-arrested-probation-violation/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

In April 2017, Kodak Black was [[indicted]] by a [[Grand juries in the United States|grand jury]] in South Carolina, and was scheduled to go on trial in April 2019 in [[Florence, South Carolina]] on a charge of first-degree criminal sexual conduct. This was later postponed.<ref>{{cite news |last=Christian |first=Matthew |date=December 6, 2018 |title=Rapper's Sex Trial to be Held in April in Florence |url=https://www.scnow.com/news/local/article_7cd2c03e-f9d2-11e8-b743-73bbd5002166.html |work=SCNow |access-date=January 23, 2019 |archive-date=December 7, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181207071509/https://www.scnow.com/news/local/article_7cd2c03e-f9d2-11e8-b743-73bbd5002166.html |url-status=live}}</ref> Also in April 2017, he appeared in court in Florida, where his anger management counselor Ramona Sanchez spoke about him disrupting her class. Sanchez said he was constantly burping during her class, and when asked to leave, he refused. When Sanchez threatened to call 911, he grabbed her phone and her wrist. The counselor recommended that Kodak Black participate in individual therapy instead of group therapy.<ref>{{cite web |title=Rapper Kodak Black Burped Excessively In Anger Management Class, Hearing Told |work=Sun Sentinel |date=April 21, 2017 |url=http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-reg-kodak-black-final-violation-probation-continues-20170420-story.html |access-date=May 4, 2017 |archive-date=April 24, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170424055850/http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-reg-kodak-black-final-violation-probation-continues-20170420-story.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

On May 4, 2017, he was sentenced for violating his house arrest to 364 days in the Broward County Jail, with the possibility of an early release if he completes a life skills course. He was released on June 5, 2017. He will remain on house arrest for one year, and five years of probation.<ref>{{cite news |last=Clarkson |first=Brett |date=May 4, 2017 |title=Kodak Black Sentenced to 364 days in Jail, but Could be Released in a Month |url=http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-sb-kodak-black-sentencing-20170503-story.html |work=Sun Sentinel |access-date=May 25, 2017 |archive-date=May 4, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170504203207/http://www.sun-sentinel.com/local/broward/fl-sb-kodak-black-sentencing-20170503-story.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== 2018–present ===

Kodak Black was arrested inside his Pembroke Pines, Florida home in January 2018 on multiple charges stemming from an [[Instagram]] live-feed video showing him passing marijuana and a gun around a small child. He initially faced seven felony charges including child neglect, grand theft of a firearm, possession of a firearm by a convicted felon, and marijuana possession.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://apnews.com/music-domestic-news-domestic-news-arts-and-entertainment-general-news-69bfc8600c4f403ea45b07137966b47f |title=Rapper Kodak Black arrested in Florida on multiple charges |work=Associated Press |date=January 19, 2018 |access-date=January 20, 2018 |archive-date=December 9, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231209125443/https://apnews.com/music-domestic-news-domestic-news-arts-and-entertainment-general-news-69bfc8600c4f403ea45b07137966b47f |url-status=live}}</ref> On February 22, 2018, three charges against Kodak Black were dropped<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.local10.com/news/local/fort-lauderdale/rapper-kodak-black-has-charges-dropped-from-broward-home-raid-arrest |title=Rapper Kodak Black has charges dropped from Broward home raid... |last=Tavss |first=Jeff |website=local10.com |access-date=March 3, 2018 |date=February 27, 2018 |archive-date=March 3, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180303225328/https://www.local10.com/news/local/fort-lauderdale/rapper-kodak-black-has-charges-dropped-from-broward-home-raid-arrest |url-status=live}}</ref> and he pleaded not guilty to the remaining two.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kodak-black-pleads-not-guilty-8221761/ |title=Kodak Black Pleads Not Guilty to Latest Home Raid Charges: Report |magazine=Billboard |access-date=March 3, 2018 |archive-date=March 1, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180301025139/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/hip-hop/8221761/kodak-black-pleads-not-guilty |url-status=live}}</ref> On April 17, he pleaded not guilty to the remaining charges, possession of a firearm by a convicted felon and possession of marijuana, and was sentenced to 364 days in prison with credit for time served.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2018/04/kodak-black-sentenced-to-one-year-in-jail-on-gun-and-marijuana-charges/ |title=Kodak Black Sentenced to One Year in Jail |website=XXL Mag |date=April 17, 2018 |access-date=May 6, 2018 |archive-date=May 6, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180506173910/http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2018/04/kodak-black-sentenced-to-one-year-in-jail-on-gun-and-marijuana-charges/ |url-status=live}}</ref> He was released on August 18, 2018.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/kodak-black-released-from-prison-after-serving-seven-months-713044/ |title=Kodak Black Has Been Released From Prison |first1=Ilana |last1=Kaplan |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]] |date=August 18, 2018 |access-date=December 1, 2018 |archive-date=December 1, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181201093340/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/kodak-black-released-from-prison-after-serving-seven-months-713044/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

While on tour in the Southeast, a South Carolinian Prosecutor announced that Kodak Black would be facing trial for first-degree criminal sexual conduct for the alleged rape in February 2016. The prosecutor said that in the summer or early fall, Kodak Black would have to return to South Carolina and face trial for the charges. They stated he faces a maximum of 30 years in prison. 12 Circuit Solicitor Ed Clements stated, "We are slowly but steadily moving toward a disposition." There were also reportedly several lesser, related charges. The office of the prosecutor stated the victim was not a minor at the time of the alleged rape.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Feit |first1=Noah |title=Hip hop star Kodak Black charged with raping high school student, SC prosecutor says |url=https://www.thestate.com/entertainment/music-news-reviews/article228857294.html |date=April 4, 2019 |website=[[State (website)|The State]] |access-date=April 5, 2019 |archive-date=April 5, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190405125109/https://www.thestate.com/entertainment/music-news-reviews/article228857294.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Connor |first1=Jay |title=Kodak Black Charged with First-Degree Sexual Assault in South Carolina, Ordered to Submit DNA Sample |url=https://thegrapevine.theroot.com/kodak-black-charged-with-first-degree-sexual-assault-in-1833834410 |website=thegrapvine.theroot.com |date=April 5, 2019 |publisher=The Grapevine |access-date=April 5, 2019 |archive-date=April 6, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190406133105/https://thegrapevine.theroot.com/kodak-black-charged-with-first-degree-sexual-assault-in-1833834410 |url-status=live}}</ref>

As of April 5, 2019, a concert promoter filed a lawsuit against Kodak Black for failing to appear at his concerts. Nicholas Fitts—the promoter—claims that Kodak Black was contractually obliged to perform for him on March 3, 2017, in New York, but did not show up. Fitts then rescheduled it for April 2017, and Kodak Black failed to appear once more. Then on a third makeup date, Kodak Black once more failed to appear. Fitts stated that the incident caused him over $500,000 in losses and hurt his reputation. His lawsuit was suing for over $500,000.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Naumann |first1=Ryan |title=Kodak Black Sued By Promoter for $500,000 Over Bailing On Concert |url=https://theblast.com/kodak-black-sued-bailing-new-york-concert/ |website=theblast.com |date=April 5, 2019 |publisher=Blast |access-date=April 5, 2019 |archive-date=April 6, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190406171115/https://theblast.com/kodak-black-sued-bailing-new-york-concert/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

While trying to re-enter the [[United States]] from [[Canada]] on April 17, 2019, Kodak Black was arrested by United States Customs and Border Protection after border authorities found marijuana and a [[Glock]] in his car. He was charged with third-degree criminal possession of a weapon, and unlawful possession of marijuana by authorities. Bail was set at either $40,000 or $20,000, he was released on the 18th. As a result of the arrest, a performance in Boston and a performance in Connecticut was canceled.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Melas |first1=Chloe |title=Rapper Kodak Black arrested |url=https://www.cnn.com/2019/04/18/entertainment/kodak-black-arrested/index.html |publisher=Central News Network |date=April 18, 2019 |access-date=April 20, 2019 |archive-date=April 19, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190419213800/https://www.cnn.com/2019/04/18/entertainment/kodak-black-arrested/index.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

Late on April 24, 2019, while on tour for his most recent album at the time, ''Dying to Live'', and while performing at a venue, officials from the [[Federal Bureau of Investigation]] and Metropolitan police entered and searched one of Kodak Black's tour buses parked at the venue. While Kodak Black was not in the vehicle at the time, the FBI found weapons in the vehicle and detained a few of Kodak Black's crew members. Allegedly, the FBI attempted to enter the club in which Kodak Black was performing, but was denied entry by the owner. [[TMZ]] stated it was "unclear" whether or not the bus was owned by Kodak Black. This came a week after his arrest at the United States{{ndash}}Canada border. It was stated Kodak Black himself did not get in trouble with law enforcement.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Shifferaw |first1=Abel |title=FBI Raided Kodak Black's Tour Buses While Rapper Was Performing in Washington D.C. |url=https://www.complex.com/music/2019/04/kodak-black-tour-bus-reportedly-raided-by-cops-fbi-in-washington-dc |website=complex.com |date=April 25, 2019 |publisher=Complex |access-date=April 25, 2019 |archive-date=April 25, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190425150425/https://www.complex.com/music/2019/04/kodak-black-tour-bus-reportedly-raided-by-cops-fbi-in-washington-dc |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Centeno |first1=Tony |title=Bus Outside Kodak Black Show Raided by FBI: Report |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/04/kodak-black-fbi-raid/ |date=April 25, 2019 |work=XXL Magazine |access-date=April 25, 2019 |archive-date=April 25, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190425142210/https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/04/kodak-black-fbi-raid/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

On May 11, 2019, while preparing to perform at Rolling Loud Miami, Kodak Black was arrested on firearm charges before he could perform. He was arrested by Miami PD and Federal Officers, and faced state and federal charges. This was nearly a month after he was arrested while entering the United States from Canada.<ref>{{cite web |last1=P. |first1=Milca |title=Kodak Black Reportedly Arrested At Rolling Loud Miami On Firearms Charges |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/196460-kodak-black-reportedly-arrested-at-rolling-loud-miami-on-firearms-charges-news |website=hotnewhiphop |date=May 12, 2019 |access-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190512020135/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kodak-black-reportedly-arrested-at-rolling-loud-miami-on-firearms-charges-news.79899.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |first=David |last=Ovalle |date=May 11, 2019 |title=Rapper Kodak Black arrested in Miami on weapons charges |url=https://www.miamiherald.com/news/local/crime/article230309874.html |work=Miami Herald |access-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-date=May 12, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190512020127/https://www.miamiherald.com/news/local/crime/article230309874.html |url-status=live}}</ref> Kodak Black was charged with two counts of making a false statement on a governmental form, this stemmed from January 2019, where he lied on the form while attempting to purchase firearms. He filed to use his $600,000 home as collateral for his $500,000 bond for the indictments and was granted the bond, being released. He reportedly faced up to 10 years in prison on the charges and pleaded not guilty on May 15. Federal prosecutors, however, attempted to revoke Kodak Black's bail, pointing to past violent crimes, such as a 2012 carjacking incident, and his possible connections to a shooting in March 2019. The arrest had the potential to cause his bond in the 2016 South Carolina rape case to be revoked. Federal prosecutors stated that he posed a danger to society due to his long history of criminal acts as well as his repeated violation of past probation rules. Kodak Black's lawyer stated that he voluntarily turned himself in upon hearing of a warrant and that he was not a danger to society due to the crime being non-violent.<ref>{{cite web |title=Rapper Kodak Black pleads not guilty to weapons charges |url=https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/rapper-kodak-black-not-guilty-weapons-charges |publisher=Fox News |date=May 16, 2019 |access-date=May 18, 2019 |archive-date=May 17, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190517164940/https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/rapper-kodak-black-not-guilty-weapons-charges |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Muhammad |first1=Latifah |title=Federal Prosecutors Reportedly Claim Kodak Black Is A Danger To Society |url=https://www.vibe.com/2019/05/prosecutors-kodak-black-danger-to-society |work=Vibe |date=May 18, 2019 |access-date=May 18, 2019 |archive-date=May 18, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190518044134/https://www.vibe.com/2019/05/prosecutors-kodak-black-danger-to-society |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Fitzgerald |first1=Trent |title=Federal Prosecutors Say Kodak Black Needs to Stay in Jail: Report |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/05/prosecutors-kodak-black-jail/ |date=May 17, 2019 |work=XXL Magazine |access-date=May 18, 2019 |archive-date=May 17, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190517232400/https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2019/05/prosecutors-kodak-black-jail/ |url-status=live}}</ref> It was reported by [[TMZ]] on November 13, 2019, that Kodak Black had taken a [[plea bargain]] and had been sentenced to 46 months in prison, a drastically shorter sentence than the 96 months that the courts had been considering as the rapper had been involved in a fight while incarcerated that involved injury to a prison guard.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.tmz.com/2019/11/13/kodak-black-sentenced-46-months-prison-federal-gun-case/ |title=Kodak Black Gets Nearly 4 Years in Prison in Federal Gun Case |website=TMZ |date=November 13, 2019 |language=en |access-date=November 13, 2019 |archive-date=November 13, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191113181003/https://www.tmz.com/2019/11/13/kodak-black-sentenced-46-months-prison-federal-gun-case/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

On March 11, 2020, Kodak Black pleaded guilty to a firearms possession case he was charged with after being detained at the Canadian-American border with a Glock. With the sentencing set for March 24, the court considered between 2 and 7 years in prison, which would run concurrently with his 46-month sentencing for lying on federal paperwork.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Centeno |first1=Tony |title=Kodak Black Pleads Guilty to Gun Possession Charge: Report |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2020/03/kodak-black-guilty-plea-gun-possession/ |website=XXL |date=March 12, 2020 |access-date=March 12, 2020 |archive-date=May 25, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200525111752/https://www.xxlmag.com/news/2020/03/kodak-black-guilty-plea-gun-possession/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

In June 2020, Kodak Black was serving his federal sentence at [[United States Penitentiary, Big Sandy]], a high-security prison in [[Inez, Kentucky]]. In October 2020, Kodak Black was transferred to [[United States Penitentiary, Thomson]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bop.gov/inmateloc/ |title=Inmate Locator |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190526132545/https://www.bop.gov/inmateloc/ |archive-date=May 26, 2019 |work=[[Federal Bureau of Prisons]] |quote=Bill K Kapri #18149-104}}</ref>

On January 19, 2021, President [[Donald Trump]] commuted Kodak Black's sentence for his 2020 conviction.<ref>{{cite magazine |title=Trump Pardons Lil Wayne, Kodak Black in Last-Minute Spree |first=Jon |last=Blistein |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/donald-trump-lil-wayne-kodak-black-1116097/ |date=January 20, 2021 |magazine=Rolling Stone |access-date=January 20, 2021 |archive-date=January 28, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210128125537/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/donald-trump-lil-wayne-kodak-black-1116097/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Kodak Black still faced charges of criminal sexual assault in Florence, South Carolina,<ref>{{cite news |last=Christian |first=Matthew |date=January 20, 2021 |title=Kodak Black's federal sentences commuted, rapper still faces charges in Florence County |url=https://scnow.com/news/local/kodak-blacks-federal-sentences-commuted-rapper-still-faces-charges-in-florence-county/article_c4c266f0-5b4c-11eb-877a-8b13cfe77cb9.html |work=SCNow |access-date=January 21, 2021 |archive-date=February 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210202083444/https://scnow.com/news/local/kodak-blacks-federal-sentences-commuted-rapper-still-faces-charges-in-florence-county/article_c4c266f0-5b4c-11eb-877a-8b13cfe77cb9.html |url-status=live}}</ref> which prosecutors were looking to "aggressively" pursue.<ref name="NewLook" /> On April 28, 2021, Kodak took a [[plea deal]] in the alleged sexual assault case and pleaded guilty to a lesser charge of first-degree assault and battery, and was sentenced to 18 months of probation.<ref>{{cite web |title=No jail time for rapper Kodak Black who pleaded guilty to lesser charge in Florence County court |url=https://www.wbtw.com/crime/pee-dee-crime/hip-hop-star-accused-of-raping-high-school-student-in-florence-could-get-plea-deal-today/ |publisher=WBTW |date=April 28, 2021 |access-date=February 12, 2022 |archive-date=February 12, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220212230431/https://www.wbtw.com/crime/pee-dee-crime/hip-hop-star-accused-of-raping-high-school-student-in-florence-could-get-plea-deal-today/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Kodak failed a drug test in mid-2021, which was a violation of his supervised release terms. He was subsequently ordered by a judge to enter a rehabilitation center for 90 days. He completed the 90 days in December of that year.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/396864-kodak-black-completes-90-day-rehab-stint-news |title=Kodak Black Is "Clean & Sober" After Getting Out Of Rehab |work=HotNewHipHop |last=Alex |first=Zidel |date=December 20, 2021 |access-date=December 28, 2021 |archive-date=December 28, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211228174058/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/kodak-black-completes-90-day-rehab-stint-news.144905.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

On January 1, 2022, he was arrested for trespassing in Pompano Beach, Florida.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Melissa |first1=Alonso |title=Kodak Black arrested for trespassing on New Year's Day |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2022/01/02/entertainment/kodak-black-arrest/index.html |website=CNN |access-date=January 5, 2022 |date=January 2, 2022 |archive-date=January 5, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220105095140/https://edition.cnn.com/2022/01/02/entertainment/kodak-black-arrest/index.html |url-status=live}}</ref>

On July 15, 2022, Kodak Black's vehicle was stopped by Florida Highway Patrol because the window tint appeared darker than the legal limit.  Police detected a smell of marijuana and searched the vehicle, finding a bag with 31 [[oxycodone]] tablets and almost $75,000 in cash.  Kodak Black was charged with trafficking in oxycodone and possession of a controlled substance.  His driver's license and vehicle tag were also expired.<ref>{{cite news |date=July 16, 2022 |title=Rapper Kodak Black is arrested on drug charges in Florida |url=https://apnews.com/article/entertainment-arrests-florida-fort-lauderdale-7d22f86d9489bb45fd09eacce98816bb |work=Associated Press |access-date=July 16, 2022 |archive-date=July 16, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220716220020/https://apnews.com/article/entertainment-arrests-florida-fort-lauderdale-7d22f86d9489bb45fd09eacce98816bb |url-status=live}}</ref> On July 20, 2022, Kodak was placed on house arrest after his arrest was said to be a violation of his supervised release.<ref>{{cite news |date=July 21, 2022 |title=Kodak Black Placed On A House Arrest |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/kodak-black-house-arrest-violating-supervised-release/ |work=XXL Magazine |access-date=July 21, 2022 |archive-date=July 21, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220721231732/https://www.xxlmag.com/kodak-black-house-arrest-violating-supervised-release/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

On December 7, 2023, Kodak Black was arrested in [[Plantation, Florida]] for possession of cocaine and tampering with evidence. A police officer initially approached him after his vehicle was blocking a roadway. Black was found with {{convert |4.1 |g |oz}} of cocaine after he tried to ingest the drug to avoid the officer discovering them.<ref>{{Cite web |first1=John |last1=Filippelli |first2=Diana |last2=Dasrath |first3=Mirna |last3=Alsharif |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/rapper-kodak-black-arrested-charges-cocaine-possession-florida-rcna128736 |title=Rapper Kodak Black arrested on charges of cocaine possession in Florida |date=December 8, 2023 |website=NBC News |access-date=December 9, 2023}}</ref> He bonded out of jail after the incident, but it was reported on December 16, 2023, that he was once again back in federal custody for violating probation.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.nbcmiami.com/news/rapper-kodak-black-in-federal-custody-after-violating-his-probation/3185720/ |title=Rapper Kodak Black in federal custody in Miami after allegedly violating probation |date=December 16, 2023}}</ref> He was later released in February 2024.<ref name=LegalHistory/> He was later reported to be embroiled in a custody battle with Miranda Johnson, the mother of two out of his five children, while also facing accusations of failure to pay [[child support]] and [[Domestic violence|domestic abuse]].<ref name=LegalHistory>{{cite news|url=https://www.miaminewtimes.com/music/a-timeline-of-kodak-blacks-arrests-alleged-crimes-and-other-legal-troubles-11178496/|title=A Timeline of Kodak Black's Legal Troubles|work=Miami New Times|access-date=May 7, 2026}}</ref>

On May 6, 2026, Kodak Black was arrested in [[Orange County, Florida]] for [[drug trafficking]] of [[MDMA]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-07 |title=Rapper Kodak Black arrested on drug trafficking charge in Central Florida, court records show - CBS Miami |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/miami/news/rapper-kodak-black-arrested-florida-drug-trafficking-orlando-area-orange-county/ |access-date=2026-05-07 |website=www.cbsnews.com |language=en-US}}</ref> The following day, he appeared in court on charges relating to the December 2023 incident and was released on $75,000 bond.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.wftv.com/news/rapper-kodak-black-bonds-out-jail-following-orlando-arrest/7039d604-0bde-4753-b228-e9e158483342/|title=Rapper Kodak Black bonds out of jail following Orlando arrest|access-date=May 8, 2026|quote=The well-known rapper was arrested [May 6, 2026] in Orlando on a drug trafficking warrant.|work=WFTV9}}</ref> According to an [[Affidavit|affidavit]], the charges stemmed from a November 2025 incident in [[Orlando, Florida|Orlando]] in which police searched his vehicle and found items that matched an [[Instagram]] post he made prior to the incident.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.wesh.com/article/instagram-posts-link-evidence-kodak-black-arrest/71240887|title=Instagram posts helped link evidence to Kodak Black's arrest, affidavit says|work=WESH2|access-date=May 8, 2026}}</ref>

