'''Jairmy Rashaan Long'''<ref name="ascap"/> known professionally as '''Lil Jairmy''', is an American rapper and songwriter from [[Houston, Texas]].<ref name="abc13"/> He is signed to [[300 Entertainment]].

== Career ==
In 2015, he released his first song "Trapped Out". In 2019, he released his first mixtape ''Excuse My Absence'' with an appearance from American rapper [[Lil Baby]].<ref name="abc13"/> In 2020, he released his project ''Can't Rush the Vibe''.<ref name="XXL1"/> In July 2021, he released his project ''Gas God'' with appearances from [[42 Dugg]], [[EST Gee]], [[Hotboii]], [[Big30]], and [[Rylo Rodriguez]].<ref name="hotnew2">{{Cite web|title=Lil Jairmy Is The "Gas God" On New Mixtape Ft. 42 Dugg, EST Gee & More
|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/341009-lil-jairmy-is-the-gas-god-on-new-mixtape-ft-42-dugg-est-gee-and-more-new-mixtape|access-date=2022-11-08|website=[[HotNewHipHop]]|language=en}}</ref> In July 2022, he released his single "Supercharge" featuring American rapper [[Moneybagg Yo]].<ref name="hotnew">{{Cite web|title=Lil Jairmy Shares "Supercharge" Single Featuring Moneybagg Yo
|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/410382-lil-jairmy-shares-supercharge-single-featuring-moneybagg-yo-new-song|access-date=2022-11-08|website=[[HotNewHipHop]]|language=en}}</ref> In September 2022, he hosted a "gas-giveaway" where he promised to fill the first 100 cars that appeared at a gas station with fuel.<ref name="abc13"/> Also In September 2022, he released his project ''Gas God 2'', the sequel to his 2021 project, with appearances from rappers [[Future (rapper)|Future]], [[Moneybagg Yo]],
[[EST Gee]], and [[Lil Keed]].<ref name="hiphopdx">{{Cite web|title=HOUSTON’S LIL JAIRMY LINKS WITH FUTURE FOR ‘ON ME’ VISUAL FROM ‘GAS GOD 2’|url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.73349/title.lil-jairmy-future-on-me-visual-gas-god-2|access-date=2022-11-08|website=[[HipHopDx]]|language=en}}</ref><ref name="thesource">{{Cite web|title=LIL JAIRMY COLLABS W/ MONEYBAGG YO, FUTURE & MORE ON ‘GAS GOD 2’|url=https://thesource.com/2022/09/11/lil-jairmy-collabs-w-moneybagg-yo-future-more-on-gas-god-2/|access-date=2022-11-08|website=[[The Source (magazine)|The Source]]|language=en}}</ref>

