Ross was briefly engaged to Lira "Galore" Mercer in 2015.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.vibe.com/news/entertainment/lira-galore-rick-ross-fix-my-life-451900/|title= Lira Galore Discusses Why She And Rick Ross Split On "Fix My Life"|work= Vibe|date= September 13, 2016|access-date= February 28, 2022|archive-date= February 28, 2022|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20220228073656/https://www.vibe.com/news/entertainment/lira-galore-rick-ross-fix-my-life-451900/|url-status= live}}</ref>

===Health===
On October 14, 2011, Ross suffered two seizures in the same day, once in the morning and again in the early evening. Following the morning seizure, he was unconscious and [[CPR]] was performed.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.17238/title.rick-ross-suffers-seizure-on-plane-reportedly-regains-consciousness|title=Rick Ross Suffers Seizure On Plane, Reportedly Regains Consciousness|date=October 14, 2011|work=[[HipHopDX]]|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150131211248/http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/news/id.17238/title.rick-ross-suffers-seizure-on-plane-reportedly-regains-consciousness|archive-date=January 31, 2015}}</ref> After suffering the second seizure, Ross was admitted to a hospital in [[Birmingham, Alabama]], where doctors ran a battery of tests. They declared him healthy. Ross attributes the episodes to a lack of sleep in the previous week.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/various-artists-3390-1280930|title=Rick Ross: 'Seizures were caused by me not getting enough sleep'|date=November 2, 2011|work=[[NME]] News|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150131221017/http://www.nme.com/news/various-artists/60153|archive-date=January 31, 2015}}</ref> Ross later noted the incident in the remix of [[Meek Mill]]'s song "[[Ima Boss]]", with the line "Had a couple seizures, call it minor setbacks / Everybody praying for me, I respect that / Woke up in the hospital, where my checks at? / Then I put 8 chains where my neck's at".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.mtv.com/news/2496364/meek-mill-ima-boss-remix-rick-ross-lil-wayne-ti-swizz-beatz/|title=Meek Mill Drops 'I'ma Boss (Remix)' W/ Rick Ross, Lil Wayne, T.I., Swizz Beatz|author=Chandler, D.L.|publisher=MTV|date=November 9, 2011|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120404035123/http://rapfix.mtv.com/2011/11/09/meek-mill-ima-boss-remix-rick-ross-lil-wayne-ti-swizz-beatz/|archive-date=April 4, 2012}}</ref>

On March 2, 2018, Ross was hospitalized after being found unresponsive in his Miami, Florida, home from a possible heart attack.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://people.com/music/rick-ross-unresponsive-florida-home/|title=Rick Ross Found Unresponsive After Emergency Crews Rush to His Miami Mansion: Report|website=People|access-date=April 25, 2018|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180401084316/http://people.com/music/rick-ross-unresponsive-florida-home/|archive-date=April 1, 2018}}</ref> Ross was on life support.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usmagazine.com/celebrity-news/news/rick-ross-hooked-up-to-life-support-report/|title=Rick Ross Hooked Up to Life Support: Report|date=March 2, 2018|website=Us Weekly|access-date=April 25, 2018|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180304061448/https://www.usmagazine.com/celebrity-news/news/rick-ross-hooked-up-to-life-support-report/|archive-date=March 4, 2018}}</ref> He was released from the hospital a few days later.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.vulture.com/2018/03/rick-ross-hospitalized-after-being-found-unresponsive.html | title=Rick Ross Released from Hospital 4 Days After Being Found Unresponsive | date=March 5, 2018 | access-date=June 1, 2023 | archive-date=June 1, 2023 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230601103638/https://www.vulture.com/2018/03/rick-ross-hospitalized-after-being-found-unresponsive.html | url-status=live }}</ref>

===Religion===
Rick Ross is a [[Christians|Christian]],<ref name="Christian">{{cite news|url=http://breathecast.christianpost.com/Christian.Music.News-Ignorance.or.Blasphemy.Secular.Rapper.Makes.Degrading.Song.About.the.Holy.Ghost/2_5837.htm|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120120184436/http://breathecast.christianpost.com/Christian.Music.News-Ignorance.or.Blasphemy.Secular.Rapper.Makes.Degrading.Song.About.the.Holy.Ghost/2_5837.htm|archive-date=January 20, 2012 |title=Ignorance or Blasphemy?|date=January 17, 2012|newspaper=[[The Christian Post]]|access-date=April 30, 2012|quote=The first verse of the song depicts Ross, a self proclaimed Christian, relishing in the riches of sitting in his expensive Bugatti as he makes a drug deal.}}</ref> and in an interview with Corey "Coco Brother" Condrey on ''[[Black Entertainment Television|Lift Every Voice]]'', he indicated that "I had told myself at one point no matter what I go through, I never question God."<ref name="Religion">{{cite news|url=http://www.rapbasement.com/videos/49967/Rick-Ross-Interview-On-A-Christian-TV-Show.html|title=Rick Ross – Interview On A Christian TV Show|year=2012|newspaper=Rap Basement|access-date=April 30, 2012|quote=I had told myself at one point no matter what I go through, I never question God.|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130424113511/http://www.rapbasement.com/videos/49967/Rick-Ross-Interview-On-A-Christian-TV-Show.html|archive-date=April 24, 2013}}</ref> In addition, Ross indicated that he [[Christian prayer|prays]] every time he goes on stage to perform.<ref name="Religion2">{{cite news|url=http://www.rapbasement.com/videos/49967/Rick-Ross-Interview-On-A-Christian-TV-Show.html|title=Rick Ross – Interview On A Christian TV Show|year=2012|newspaper=Rap Basement|access-date=April 30, 2012|quote=Every time I go on stage, you know what I'm saying, I say a prayer.|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130424113511/http://www.rapbasement.com/videos/49967/Rick-Ross-Interview-On-A-Christian-TV-Show.html|archive-date=April 24, 2013}}</ref>

===Correctional officer photos===
In July 2008, ''[[The Smoking Gun]]'' produced details linking Ross's social security number to an 18-month stint as a correctional officer at the South Florida Reception Center, along with a photograph first publicized by [[Media Take Out]] purporting to be Ross in his [[Prison officer|correctional officer]] uniform.<ref name="Rick Ross CO" /> Ross initially denied that the photograph was of him,<ref>{{cite news|last=Reid|first=Shaheem|title=Rick Ross Reaffirms Gangster Past In New Freestyle, Despite Report That He Worked As Prison Guard|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/1591284/rick-ross-reaffirms-gangster-past-in-new-freestyle-despite-report-that-he-worked-as-prison-guard/|publisher=MTV News|date=July 22, 2008|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080828040235/http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1591284/20080722/ross__rick__rap_.jhtml|archive-date=August 28, 2008}}</ref> but after overwhelming evidence of his past came into the public's eye, Ross later admitted that he did work as a correctional officer in Florida for 18 months between 1995 and 1997.<ref>{{cite magazine|last=Burgess|first=Omar|title=Rick Ross Admits Correctional Officer Past|url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.7847/title.rick-ross-admits-correctional-officer-past|magazine=Hip Hop DX|date=October 7, 2008|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20081201090640/http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/news/id.7847/title.rick-ross-admits-correctional-officer-past|archive-date=December 1, 2008}}</ref> In a 2008 interview with AllHipHop.com,<ref>{{cite web |last1=Watkins |first1=Grouchy Greg |title=Freeway Ricky Ross: Name Check |url=https://allhiphop.com/features/freeway-ricky-ross-name-check/ |website=AllHipHop |access-date=February 28, 2022 |date=August 1, 2008|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090331072305/http://allhiphop.com/stories/features/archive/2008/08/01/20354914.aspx|archive-date=March 31, 2009}}</ref> [[Ricky Ross (drug trafficker)|"Freeway" Ricky Ross]] claimed offense that Roberts used his name and identity when he learned that ''The Smoking Gun'' posted documents revealing Roberts' previous employment as a Florida correctional officer.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.thesmokinggun.com/archive/years/2008/0721081rickross1.html|title=Screw Rick Ross – TheSmokingGun.com|work=The Smoking Gun|access-date=November 22, 2014|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100723013054/http://www.thesmokinggun.com/archive/years/2008/0721081rickross1.html|archive-date=July 23, 2010}}</ref>

===Drive-by shooting===
On January 27, 2013, while celebrating his 37th birthday, Ross and his girlfriend were the targets of a [[drive-by shooting]] in [[Fort Lauderdale, Florida]]. Neither Ross nor his girlfriend were hurt, but they ended up crashing their car into an apartment in an attempt to escape the shooting.<ref>{{cite web |last=Haskell |first=Josh |url=https://abcnews.go.com/blogs/entertainment/2013/01/rapper-rick-ross-target-of-drive-by-shooting/ |title=Rapper Rick Ross Target of Drive-By Shooting |publisher=ABC News |date=January 28, 2013 |access-date=August 6, 2013 |archive-date=August 21, 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130821083337/http://abcnews.go.com/blogs/entertainment/2013/01/rapper-rick-ross-target-of-drive-by-shooting/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Business ventures===
As of 2017, Ross owned several different [[Wingstop]] restaurant locations.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://allhiphop.com/news/rick-ross-opens-new-wingstop-decatur/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170322204046/https://allhiphop.com/2017/01/26/rick-ross-opens-new-wingstop-decatur/|access-date=February 28, 2022|title=Rick Ross Opens New Wingstop In Decatur|archive-date=March 22, 2017|website=All HipHop|date=January 26, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://thesource.com/2016/07/04/rick-ross-makes-big-moves-to-expand-his-franchise/|title=Rick Ross Makes Big Moves To Expand His Franchise|date=July 4, 2016|website=The Source|access-date=April 25, 2018|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201030620/http://thesource.com/2016/07/04/rick-ross-makes-big-moves-to-expand-his-franchise/|archive-date=December 1, 2017}}</ref> Wingstop is a fast-food chain specializing in chicken wings.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Wingstop |title=About Us |url=https://www.wingstop.com/about-us |website=Wingstop |access-date=May 8, 2019 |archive-date=May 9, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190509172259/https://www.wingstop.com/about-us |url-status=live }}</ref> When [[Don Lemon]] was fired from CNN in April 2023, Ross offered him a job, saying, "For some reason, I believe you know what you doing with the [[lemon pepper wings]]. So man, just send over your résumé."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Marr |first=Madeline |date=April 25, 2023 |title=Don Lemon just got fired, but this Miami rapper has a job for him: 'Send your resume' |url=https://www.miamiherald.com/miami-com/miami-com-news/article274693376.html |access-date=April 25, 2023 |website=www.miamiherald.com |archive-date=April 26, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230426083300/https://www.miamiherald.com/miami-com/miami-com-news/article274693376.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Legal issues==
[[File:Rick Ross mug shot.jpg|thumb|150px|[[Mug shot]] of Ross, 2008]]
In January 2008, Ross was arrested on gun and marijuana charges. During a deposition of Officer Rey Hernandez, a Miami Beach police officer who arrested Ross, Ross's lawyer, Allan Zamren, asked Hernandez why Ross's case was assigned to the gang task force. The officer stated that it was because Ross claimed affiliation with [[Triple C's]] (aka Carol City Cartel), and other known gang members. Zamren pressed Hernandez for a personal link between Ross and the gang members, but the officer did not provide proof.<ref>{{cite news|title=Rick Ross' Own Lawyer De-Values |url=http://highbridnation.com/2009/02/10/rick-ross-own-lawyer-de-values-his-gangsta/ |publisher=Highbridnation.com |date=February 10, 2009 |access-date=March 24, 2009 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090213102229/http://highbridnation.com/2009/02/10/rick-ross-own-lawyer-de-values-his-gangsta |archive-date=February 13, 2009 }}</ref>

In August 2008, YouTube entertainer [[DJ Vlad]] filed a lawsuit against Ross for assault and battery. Vlad claimed Ross organized an ambush on him at the 2008 Ozone Awards in [[Houston]], Texas for asking questions about his past as a correctional officer.<ref>{{cite news|last=Kaufman|first=Gil|title=DJ Vlad Files $4 Million Lawsuit Against Rick Ross Over Alleged Ozone Awards Beatdown|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/1592890/dj-vlad-files-4-million-lawsuit-against-rick-ross-over-alleged-ozone-awards-beatdown/|publisher=MTV News|date=August 15, 2008|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080828040710/http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1592890/20080815/ross__rick__rap_.jhtml|archive-date=August 28, 2008|access-date=February 28, 2022}}</ref>

In June 2010 "Freeway" Ricky Ross sued Ross for using his name,<ref name="Freeway Rick Ross sues Rick Ross">{{cite web|url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.11543/title.freeway-ricky-ross-files-lawsuit-against-rapper-rick-ross|title=Freeway Rick Ross files lawsuit|last=Harling|first=Danielle|date=June 25, 2010|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140103035148/http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/news/id.11543/title.freeway-ricky-ross-files-lawsuit-against-rapper-rick-ross|archive-date=January 3, 2014}}</ref> filing a [[copyright infringement]] [[lawsuit]] in a California federal court.<ref name="Freeway Rick Ross sues Rick Ross" /> [[Jay-Z]] had been called to testify in the lawsuit, as he was CEO of Def Jam when Ross/Roberts was signed.<ref name="Freeway Rick Ross sues Rick Ross" /> "Freeway" Ricky Ross, a reformed drug kingpin, sought $10 million in damages in his lawsuit.<ref name="Freeway Rick Ross sues Rick Ross" /> Also, Freeway Ricky Ross threatened to block the release of Ross's album, ''[[Teflon Don (album)|Teflon Don]].''{{citation needed|date=August 2024}}

A week after the lawsuit was filed, Rick Ross responded to the charges: "It's like owning a restaurant, you're gonna have a few slip and falls. You get lawsuits, you deal with them, and get them out your way&nbsp;... sometimes you lose."<ref name="Rapper Rick Ross Gets Legal Victory, Replies To $10 Mil Lawsuit">{{cite web|url=http://allhiphop.com/stories/news/archive/2010/07/02/22284307.aspx|title=Rapper Rick Ross Gets Legal Victory, Replies To $10 Mil Lawsuit|last=Strong, Bostick|first=Nolan, Octavia|access-date=September 12, 2010|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100706145646/http://www.allhiphop.com/stories/news/archive/2010/07/02/22284307.aspx|archive-date=July 6, 2010}}</ref> He denied rumors that he would change his name to "Ricky Rozay" as a consequence of the lawsuit. The lawsuit was thrown out of court on July 3, 2010.<ref name="SuitThrown">{{cite web|url=http://theurbandaily.com/gossip-news/billjohnson/freeway-ricky-ross-lawsuit-against-rick-ross-thrown-out/|title=Freeway Ricky Ross' Lawsuit Against Rick Ross Thrown Out|last=Johnson|first=Bill|date=July 6, 2010|access-date=September 12, 2010|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120312171244/http://theurbandaily.com/gossip-news/billjohnson/freeway-ricky-ross-lawsuit-against-rick-ross-thrown-out/|archive-date=March 12, 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.vulture.com/2010/11/the_drug_dealer_rick_ross_has.html |magazine=Vulture |title=The Drug Dealer Rick Ross Has Lost His Lawsuit Against the Rapper Rick Ross |date=November 5, 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111229053922/http://nymag.com/daily/entertainment/2010/11/the_drug_dealer_rick_ross_has.html |archive-date=December 29, 2011 |url-status=live }}</ref> The album ''Teflon Don'' was released as scheduled on July 20, 2010.

A federal judge ruled that the case should be refiled in California state court because it fell under California state law. "Freeway" Ricky Ross refiled the case with the State of California and the federal case is on appeal in the [[United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit]].<ref name="SuitThrown"/> The state case was filed in 2011 in California.

"Freeway" Ricky Ross refiled in Los Angeles Superior Court with publicity rights claims. Trial was set for early May 2012. The case was dismissed by a judge in the Los Angeles Superior Court.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/2497235/freeway-rick-ross-court-date-with-rick-ross/|title='Freeway' Rick Ross Will Take On Rick Ross In Court Again |website=[[MTV]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140103030721/http://rapfix.mtv.com/2012/02/29/freeway-rick-ross-court-date-with-rick-ross/ |archive-date=January 3, 2014 |url-status=dead|date=February 29, 2012|access-date=February 28, 2022}}</ref>

The California State case was updated with a motion in Freeway Rick Ross's favor as to [[Warner Bros. Records]] and their use of the name and image Rick Ross in July 2012.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/rick-ross-freeway-ricky-warner-bros-sue-maybach-music-351204/ |title=Rick Ross Vs. Ricky "Freeway" Ross: Judge Rejects Warner Bros. Records' Motion to Dismiss |work=The Hollywood Reporter |first=Eriq |last=Gardner|access-date=February 28, 2022|date=July 18, 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130127180836/http://www.billboard.biz/bbbiz/industry/legal-and-management/rick-ross-vs-ricky-freeway-ross-judge-rejects-1007617352.story |archive-date=January 27, 2013 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On December 30, 2013, the court ruled in favor of the rapper Rick Ross, allowing him to keep the name based on a [[First Amendment to the United States Constitution|First Amendment]] ruling.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/freeway-ricky-ross-rick-ross-667879/ |work=The Hollywood Reporter |first=Eriq |last=Gardner |title='Freeway' Ricky Ross vs. Rick Ross: First Amendment Protects Hip-Hop Persona |date=December 30, 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140309134858/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/thr-esq/freeway-ricky-ross-rick-ross-667879 |archive-date=March 9, 2014|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2011, the rapper Teflon Don filed a [[trademark infringement]] lawsuit against Ross for the use of the name as an album title.<ref name="Memphis Rap 2011-08-29">{{cite news|url=http://www.memphisrap.com/2011/08/29/exclusive-rick-ross-dj-khaled-def-jam-named-in-infringement-lawsuit-by-teflon-don/|title=Freeway Exclusive: Rick Ross, DJ Khaled, Def Jam Named In Infringement Lawsuit by Teflon Don|date=August 29, 2011|access-date=March 1, 2013|archive-date=January 29, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130129072202/http://www.memphisrap.com/2011/08/29/exclusive-rick-ross-dj-khaled-def-jam-named-in-infringement-lawsuit-by-teflon-don/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Rick Ross, DJ Khaled & More Being Sued for 'Teflon Don' Name">{{cite news|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/rick-ross-dj-khaled-more-being-sued-for-teflon-don-name-467680/|title=Rick Ross, DJ Khaled & More Being Sued for 'Teflon Don' Name|last=Ramirez|first=Erika|date=August 29, 2011|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130316052136/http://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/the-juice/467680/rick-ross-dj-khaled-more-being-sued-for-teflon-don-name|archive-date=March 16, 2013|access-date=February 28, 2022}}</ref>

On March 26, 2011, Ross was arrested in Shreveport for possession of [[marijuana]]. According to the police records, a strong odor of marijuana was detected from his room at the Hilton in Downtown Shreveport.<ref>{{cite news |author=Clemons, Tracy |title=Rapper and NFL star separately arrested in Shreveport |url=https://www.ksla.com/story/14326804/rapper-known-as-rick-ross-arrested-in-shreveport/ |work=KSLA |date=March 26, 2011 |access-date=February 28, 2022 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120307171443/http://www.ksla.com/Global/story.asp?S=14326804 |archive-date=March 7, 2012  }}</ref> Ross was arrested on June 27, 2014, in Greensboro, N.C., following his performance at the 2014 SuperJam at the Greensboro Coliseum. The arrest stemmed from a year-old warrant for another North Carolina arrest related to marijuana possession; Ross reportedly failed to appear in court for that violation in 2013.<ref>{{cite magazine|title=Rick Ross Arrested in North Carolina on Outstanding Warrant|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/rick-ross-arrested-in-north-carolina-on-outstanding-warrant-6141058/|magazine=billboard|date=June 28, 2014|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150617215342/http://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/the-juice/6141058/rick-ross-arrested-in-north-carolina-on-outstanding-warrant|archive-date=June 17, 2015}}</ref>

On June 24, 2015, Rick Ross and his bodyguard were arrested in [[Fayette County, Georgia]] on kidnapping and assault charges. Both were accused for forcing a landskeeper into a guesthouse and beating him in the head with a handgun, allegedly over money he owed Ross.<ref>{{cite web|title=RICK ROSS ARRESTED FOR KIDNAPPING ASSAULT|url=http://www.thedailybeast.com/cheats/2015/06/24/rick-ross-booked-for-kidnapping-assault.html|website=The Daily Beast|date=June 24, 2015|access-date=June 25, 2015|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150627061347/http://www.thedailybeast.com/cheats/2015/06/24/rick-ross-booked-for-kidnapping-assault.html|archive-date=June 27, 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=Rapper Rick Ross Arrested on Kidnapping, Assault Charges|url=https://abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/wireStory/rapper-rick-ross-arrested-kidnapping-assault-charges-31990584|website=abc News|access-date=June 25, 2015|url-status=live|archive-url=http://archive.wikiwix.com/cache/20140414003650/http://abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/wireStory/rapper-rick-ross-arrested-kidnapping-assault-charges-31990584|archive-date=April 14, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|title=Rick Ross Arrested on Kidnapping, Assault Charges|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/rick-ross-arrested-kidnapping-assault-charges-6605814/|magazine=Billboard|date = June 24, 2015|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150628194629/http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/6605814/rick-ross-arrested-kidnapping-assault-charges?mobile_redirection=false|archive-date=June 28, 2015}}</ref> On April 4, 2017, Ross pled no contest to a felony count of aggravated assault. The other felony charges were dropped. Ross was sentenced to time served in jail, having already been incarcerated for a week and was also ordered to pay a $10,000 fine.{{citation needed|date=August 2024}}

Ross was sentenced as a first-time felony offender; and, upon payment of the fine, the conviction was erased from his record. Ross pled no contest to 5 misdemeanors: assault, battery, two counts of pointing a pistol at someone, and possession of less than 1 oz of cannabis. For the five misdemeanors, he was given a total of 60 months probation.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tmz.com/2017/04/04/rick-ross-plea-deal-kidnapping-case/|title=RICK ROSS GETS SWEET PLEA DEAL IN KIDNAPPING CASE|website=TMZ|date=April 4, 2017 |access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180221043214/http://amp.tmz.com/2017/04/04/rick-ross-plea-deal-kidnapping-case|archive-date=February 21, 2018}}</ref>

==Controversies==
===Feud with 50 Cent===
{{Multiple issues|section=yes|
{{Tone|section|date=August 2022}}
{{Update section|date=August 2022}}
}}
In January 2009, Ross started a feud with rapper [[50 Cent]] because he supposedly looked at him the wrong way at the [[BET Hip Hop Awards]] in 2008. 50 Cent told news sources that he did not remember seeing Ross there.<ref>{{cite news|title=How feud Started Rick Ross and 50 Cent |url=http://www.vibe.com/news/news_headlines/2009/01/50_cent_vs_rick_ross_video/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090203122223/http://www.vibe.com/news/news_headlines/2009/01/50_cent_vs_rick_ross_video/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=February 3, 2009 |publisher=Vide.com |date=February 7, 2009 |access-date=March 16, 2009 }}</ref> In late January, Ross's "Mafia Music" was leaked onto the internet. There were several lines that seemed to disparage 50 Cent. Days later, 50 Cent released "Officer Ricky (Go Head, Try Me)" in response to Ross's remarks.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Muhammad |first=Latifah MuhammadLatifah |date=2009-01-30 |title=50 Cent Responds to Rick Ross With 'Officer Ricky' |url=https://theboombox.com/50-cent-responds-to-rick-ross-with-officer-ricky/ |access-date=2026-08-29 |website=The Boombox |language=en}}</ref>

Within a month, 50 Cent uploaded a video entitled "Warning Shot", wherein he stated: "Rick Ross, I'mma fuck your life up for fun." In addition, 50 Cent released the first of a series of "Officer Ricky" cartoons. Early in February, 50 Cent produced and posted a video to YouTube in which he interviewed "Tia", the mother of one of Ross's children. She confirmed that he had been a correctional officer and claimed his whole persona was inauthentic.<ref>{{cite web |title=50 Cent – Interviews Rick Ross' Baby Mama |url=https://hiphopdx.com/videos/id.2138/title.50-cent-interviews-rick-ross-baby-mama |website=HipHopDX |access-date=February 28, 2022 |date=February 2, 2009|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121001091702/http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/videos/id.2138 |archive-date=October 1, 2012 }}</ref> On February 5, 2009, [[The Game (rapper)|The Game]], who 50 Cent has a long-standing "beef" with, called in to [[Seattle]] R&B station [[KUBE (FM)|KUBE]]. When asked about the beef between 50 Cent and Ross, Game sided with 50 Cent, opining that things were not looking good for Ross. He offered to help, stating, "Rick Ross, holla at your boy, man" and "50 eating you, boy."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/1604407/game-takes-sides-in-50-cent-rick-ross-beef/|title=Game Takes Sides In 50 Cent|work=MTV News|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090823024332/http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1604407/20090205/ross__rick__rap_.jhtml|archive-date=August 23, 2009}}</ref>

On his album ''[[Deeper Than Rap]]'', Ross references 50 Cent in the song "In Cold Blood". A video for the song was released that portrayed 50 Cent's mock funeral. Upon release, Ross stated that he had ended 50 Cent's career.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/1609554/rick-ross-buries-50-cent-in-cold-blood-video/|title=Rick Ross Buries 50 Cent In 'Cold Blood'|work=MTV News |access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090721093932/http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1609554/20090420/ross__rick__rap_.jhtml|archive-date=July 21, 2009}}</ref> That same day, Ross released a new diss track called "Push 'Em Over The Edge". The next day, 50 Cent released the controversial video "A Psychic Told Me", dissing [[DJ Khaled]]. On February 12, 50 Cent responded to Ross with "Tia Told Me", which was released alongside Lloyd Banks' response "Officer Down" and Tony Yayo's "Somebody Snitched".{{citation needed|date=August 2024}}

In an interview, 50 Cent said Ross is "Albert From ''[[CB4]]''. You ever seen the movie? He's Albert," he added. "It never gets worse than this. You get a guy that was a correctional officer come out and base his entire career on writing material from a drug dealer's perspective."<ref>[http://www.ballerstatus.com/2009/03/03/50-cent-says-rick-ross-is-gusto-from-cb4-laughs-off-ross-sales-predictions/ 50 Cent Says Rick Ross Is 'Gusto From CB4', Laughs Off Ross' Sales Predictions] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100619085851/http://www.ballerstatus.com/2009/03/03/50-cent-says-rick-ross-is-gusto-from-cb4-laughs-off-ross-sales-predictions/ |date=June 19, 2010 }} BallerStatus.com</ref>

On January 30, 2013, 50 Cent claimed via Twitter that the drive-by shooting that Ross experienced on his birthday two days ago was "staged", reigniting the feud.<ref>{{cite news|last=Sieczkowski|first=Cavan|title=50 Cent Claims Rick Ross Shooting Was 'Staged'|url=https://www.huffpost.com/entry/50-cent-rick-ross-shooting-staged_n_2581245|newspaper=[[HuffPost]]|date=January 30, 2013|url-status=live|access-date=February 28, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130209200009/http://www.huffingtonpost.com/2013/01/30/50-cent-rick-ross-shooting-staged_n_2581245.html|archive-date=February 9, 2013}}</ref>

A year later, on March 28, 2014, Rick Ross was asked about his feud with 50 Cent. He stated that he does not wish to speak on him anymore, and that he is done with the feud.<ref>{{cite magazine|last=Harling|first=Danielle|title=Rick Ross "Through Talking About" 50 Cent|url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.28096/title.rick-ross-through-talking-about-50-cent|magazine=HipHopDX|access-date=February 28, 2022|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140401123036/http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/news/id.28096/title.rick-ross-through-talking-about-50-cent|archive-date=April 1, 2014}}</ref>

His feud with 50 Cent resurfaced in 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/461790-meek-mill-disses-50-cent-on-gave-em-hope-news|title=50 Cent and Rick Ross beef resurfacing|publisher=Hot New Hip Hop|date=January 16, 2016|access-date=January 17, 2016|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160119185111/http://www.hotnewhiphop.com/meek-mill-disses-50-cent-on-gave-em-hope-news.19660.html|archive-date=January 19, 2016}}</ref> In January, Ross's MMG record-label artist [[Meek Mill]]
defended his mentor and criticised 50 on his ''4/4'' EP.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.rap-up.com/2016/02/01/50-cent-disses-meek-mill-at-nyc-show/ |title=50 Cent Disses Meek Mill: 'All You Can Do Is Run to Nicki' |magazine=Rap-Up |access-date=March 15, 2017 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170415142357/http://www.rap-up.com/2016/02/01/50-cent-disses-meek-mill-at-nyc-show/ |archive-date=April 15, 2017  }}</ref>

===Lyric controversy===
In a line on rapper [[Rocko (rapper)|Rocko]]'s 2013 song "[[U.O.E.N.O.]]", Rick Ross raps the line, "Put molly all in her champagne / She ain't even know it / I took her home and I enjoyed that / She ain't even know it." A petition containing 72,000 signatures was presented to [[Reebok]], demanding they drop Ross as a spokesman for the lyrics which appeared to condone [[date rape]]. Ross has apologized for the lyrics, claiming they weren't about rape.<ref>{{cite news| url= http://www.3news.co.nz/Rick-Ross-rape-lyric-apology-not-accepted/tabid/418/articleID/293110/Default.aspx| work= 3 News NZ| title= Rick Ross rape lyric apology not accepted| date= April 5, 2013| url-status=live| archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20131224121936/http://www.3news.co.nz/Rick-Ross-rape-lyric-apology-not-accepted/tabid/418/articleID/293110/Default.aspx| archive-date= December 24, 2013| df= mdy-all}}</ref>

On April 11, 2013, one month after the song's release, Ross was dropped by Reebok.<ref>{{cite news|title=RICK ROSS REEBOK GIVES RAPPER THE BOOT|url=https://www.tmz.com/2013/04/11/reebok-dumps-rick-ross-drops/|work=TMZ|access-date=April 11, 2013|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130413111416/http://www.tmz.com/2013/04/11/reebok-dumps-rick-ross-drops/|archive-date=April 13, 2013}}</ref> Reebok stated, "while we do not believe that Rick Ross condones sexual assault, we are very disappointed he has yet to display an understanding of the seriousness of this issue or an appropriate level of remorse."  They continued on to say, "at this time, it is in everyone's best interest for Reebok to end its partnership with Mr. Ross."<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/rick-ross-loses-reebok-endorsement-over-rape-lyrics-233402/|title=Rick Ross Loses Reebok Endorsement Over 'Rape' Lyrics|last=Danton|first=Eric|date=April 12, 2013|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|access-date=May 7, 2019|archive-date=May 7, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190507172127/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/rick-ross-loses-reebok-endorsement-over-rape-lyrics-233402/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|first=Sean |last=Michaels |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2013/apr/12/rick-ross-loses-reebok-deal|title=Rick Ross loses Reebok deal over 'date rape' verse|date=April 12, 2013|website=[[The Guardian]]|access-date=May 7, 2019|archive-date=May 7, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190507172125/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2013/apr/12/rick-ross-loses-reebok-deal|url-status=live}}</ref>

Though Ross apologized for the lyrics, he also argued that his lyrics were misinterpreted because he did not directly use the word "rape". He said, "You know I would never use the term rape in my records&nbsp;... in reality some people do these things, and shouldn't it be brought to light so young women can protect themselves?!" He continued on Twitter, "I would never use the term 'rape' in my records and as far as my camp. Hip-Hop don't condone that, the streets don't condone that, nobody condones that."<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.vice.com/en/article/question-of-the-day-is-rick-ross-a-misogynist/|title=Question Of The Day – Is Rick Ross a Misogynist?|last=Gadiano|first=Jerry|date=April 15, 2013|website=[[Vice.com|Vice]]|access-date=May 7, 2019|archive-date=May 8, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190508022754/https://www.vice.com/en_us/article/6wg4y6/question-of-the-day-is-rick-ross-a-misogynist|url-status=live}}</ref>

A 2013 Ross concert organized by the student association of [[Carleton University]] was cancelled after protests that his lyrics promote [[rape culture]].<ref>{{cite web |first=Jakob |last=Kuzyk |url=http://www.charlatan.ca/2013/04/former-cusa-prez-running-company-behind-rick-ross-concert/ |title=Rick Ross concert completely cancelled following criticism |date=April 4, 2013 |website=Charlatan |access-date=August 6, 2013 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130523093356/http://charlatan.ca/2013/04/former-cusa-prez-running-company-behind-rick-ross-concert/ |archive-date=May 23, 2013  }}</ref> Rocko later dropped the Rick Ross verse in order to get radio play.<ref>{{cite news| url= http://www.3news.co.nz/Rocko-replaces-Rick-Ross-rap/tabid/418/articleID/293956/Default.aspx| work= 3 News NZ| title= Rocko replaces Rick Ross rap| date= April 12, 2013| url-status=live| archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20140102193644/http://www.3news.co.nz/Rocko-replaces-Rick-Ross-rap/tabid/418/articleID/293956/Default.aspx| archive-date= January 2, 2014| df= mdy-all}}</ref>

