'''Aubrey Drake Graham''' (born October 24, 1986) is a Canadian<!--Note:While Drake is a dual citizen of Canada and the United States of America, he gained notability as a Canadian and mainly identifies with his Canadian nationality--> rapper and singer.<!--Note:Keep most notable professions in lead per [[MOS:ROLEBIO]].--> Often referred to as one of the greatest rappers of all time, he is credited with popularizing [[Contemporary R&B|R&B]] sensibilities in [[hip-hop]] music through [[rap-singing]]. Drake first gained recognition as [[Jimmy Brooks]] in the [[CTV Television Network|CTV]] teen drama series ''[[Degrassi: The Next Generation]]'' (2001–2008) and began his music career by [[Unsigned artist|independently]] releasing the mixtapes ''[[Room for Improvement (mixtape)|Room for Improvement]]'' (2006), ''[[Comeback Season (mixtape)|Comeback Season]]'' (2007), and ''[[So Far Gone (mixtape)|So Far Gone]]'' (2009), before signing with [[Young Money Entertainment]].<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/drake-signs-to-young-money-distribution-by-universal-republic-268244/ |title=Drake Signs To Young Money, Distribution By Universal Republic |magazine=Billboard |date=June 30, 2009 |access-date=March 5, 2022 |archive-date=March 6, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220306015220/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/drake-signs-to-young-money-distribution-by-universal-republic-268244/ |url-status=live}}</ref> 

Drake's debut album, ''[[Thank Me Later]]'' (2010), debuted atop the [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]] and included his breakthrough hit "[[Best I Ever Had]]". He followed it with the albums ''[[Take Care]]'' (2011) and ''[[Nothing Was the Same]]'' (2013); the former was included on ''[[Rolling Stone]]''{{'s}} "[[Rolling Stone's 500 Greatest Albums of All Time|500 Greatest Albums of All Time]]" list. His fourth studio album, ''[[Views (album)|Views]]'' (2016), led the ''Billboard'' 200 for 13 weeks. Its second single, "[[One Dance]]", became the [[List of Spotify streaming records|first song to surpass 1 billion streams]] on [[Spotify]]. In 2018, Drake released his fifth studio album, ''[[Scorpion (Drake album)|Scorpion]]'', spending [[List of Billboard Hot 100 chart achievements and milestones#Most weeks at number one in a calendar year|29 weeks]] atop the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] with its singles: "[[God's Plan (song)|God's Plan]]", "[[Nice for What]]", and "[[In My Feelings]]". Throughout the 2020s, Drake amassed six US number-one albums, including ''[[Certified Lover Boy]]'' (2021) and ''[[Iceman (album)|Iceman]]'' (2026), which respectively spawned [[List of Billboard Hot 100 chart achievements and milestones#Most top ten songs from one album|nine and ten US top ten songs]]. In 2026, he became the first artist to occupy the top three spots on the ''Billboard'' 200.{{efn|Aided by the simultaneously released 2026 albums ''[[Iceman (album)|Iceman]]'', ''[[Habibti (album)|Habibti]]'' and ''[[Maid of Honour (album)|Maid of Honour]]'', respectively.}}

As an entrepreneur, Drake founded the record label [[OVO Sound]], production company [[DreamCrew]], and the fragrance house Better World. In 2013, he became the "global ambassador" of the [[Toronto Raptors]], joining their executive committee and later obtaining naming rights to their practice facility [[OVO Athletic Centre]]. In 2016, he began collaborating with [[Brent Hocking]] on the [[bourbon whiskey]] [[Virginia Black Whiskey|Virginia Black]]. Drake is a co-owner of the gaming organization [[100 Thieves]], and heads the OVO fashion label and the Nocta collaboration with [[Nike, Inc.]] His 2015 partnership with [[Apple Music]] has been credited with the successful launch of that platform. Drake has received widespread media coverage due to his extravagant lifestyle and [[rap feud]]s, including [[Drake–Kanye West feud|with Kanye West]] and [[Drake–Kendrick Lamar feud|with Kendrick Lamar]].

Among the world's [[List of best-selling music artists|best-selling music artists]], with over 170&nbsp;million units sold, Drake is also ranked as the highest-certified [[List of highest-certified music artists in the United States|digital singles]] artist in the United States.<ref name="billboard riaa2">{{cite magazine |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/drake-riaa-top-digital-singles-artist-8463480/ |title=Drake Certified as RIAA's New Top Digital Singles Artist |last=Mitchell |first=Gail |magazine=Billboard |date=June 29, 2018 |access-date=March 5, 2022 |archive-date=March 6, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220306015210/https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/drake-riaa-top-digital-singles-artist-8463480/ |url-status=live}}</ref> [[List of awards and nominations received by Drake|His accolades]] include 5 [[Grammy Award]]s, 6 [[American Music Awards]], [[Billboard Music Award#Most wins|41 ''Billboard'' Music Awards]], 2 [[Brit Awards]], and 3 [[Juno Awards]]. ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' named him the [[Billboard Decade-End#2010s|Artist of the Decade (2010s)]], the [[List of highest-grossing live music artists#Hip-hop|highest-grossing hip-hop touring artist]], and the [[Billboard's Greatest Pop Stars#21st Century|fourth greatest pop star of the 21st century]]. He has achieved [[Billboard 200#Most number-one albums|15 ''Billboard'' 200 number-one albums]] and [[Artists with the most number-ones on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100 chart|14 ''Billboard'' Hot 100 number-one singles]];{{efn|Drake appears on Travis Scott's number-one single "[[Sicko Mode]]"; he was credited for a brief period on Apple Music and retains credit on the [[YouTube]] music video, but not on any other platform including the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]].}} both rank as a record among male solo artists. He additionally has the most number-one singles on the [[R&B/Hip-Hop Airplay]], [[Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Songs]], [[Hot Rap Songs]], and [[Rhythmic Airplay]] charts.<!-- Leave space for TOC limit -->

