The following is a list of cast members who have portrayed characters appearing in [[20th Century Fox]]'s [[X-Men (film series)|''X-Men'' film series]], based upon the [[Marvel Comics]] superhero team [[X-Men|of the same name]] and its related characters.

The first three films in the series are ''[[X-Men (film)|X-Men]]'' (2000), ''[[X2 (film)|X2]]'' (2003), and ''[[X-Men: The Last Stand]]'' (2006), starring [[Hugh Jackman]] as [[Logan (film character)|James "Logan" Howlett / Wolverine]], [[Patrick Stewart]] as [[Charles Xavier (film character)|Charles Xavier / Professor X]], [[Ian McKellen]] as [[Magneto (film character)|Erik Lehnsherr / Magneto]], [[Famke Janssen]] as [[Jean Grey]], [[Halle Berry]] as [[Storm (Marvel Comics)|Ororo Munroe / Storm]], [[Anna Paquin]] as [[Rogue (Marvel Comics)|Marie D'Ancanto / Rogue]], [[James Marsden]] as [[Cyclops (Marvel Comics)|Scott Summers / Cyclops]], [[Shawn Ashmore]] as [[Iceman (Marvel Comics)|Bobby Drake / Iceman]], and [[Rebecca Romijn]] as [[Mystique (film character)|Raven Darkhölme / Mystique]]. [[Daniel Cudmore]] portrays [[Colossus (character)|Piotr Rasputin / Colossus]] in the last two films, while [[Elliot Page]]{{efn|name=Elliot|Credited as Ellen Page; ''The Last Stand'' and ''Days of Future Past'' were released before Page came out as [[transgender]].<ref name="PageTransgender" />}}<!--per wp:GENDERID and consistent with Juno and Freeheld articles--> and [[Kelsey Grammer]] star as [[Kitty Pryde]] and [[Beast (Marvel Comics)|Hank McCoy / Beast]], respectively, in the latter. Jackman also stars in a trilogy of films centered on Wolverine, consisting of ''[[X-Men Origins: Wolverine]]'' (2009), ''[[The Wolverine (film)|The Wolverine]]'' (2013), and ''[[Logan (film)|Logan]]'' (2017), where he is joined by Stewart as Xavier.

[[James McAvoy]], [[Michael Fassbender]], [[Jennifer Lawrence]], and [[Nicholas Hoult]] star in ''[[X-Men: First Class]]'' (2011) as younger versions of Xavier, Lehnsherr, Darkhölme, and McCoy, respectively, while [[Lucas Till]] appears as [[Havok (character)|Alex Summers / Havok]]. ''[[X-Men: Days of Future Past]]'' (2014) features both the original cast (except for Romijn) and the new actors, while also introducing [[Evan Peters]] as [[Peter Maximoff|Peter Maximoff / Quicksilver]]. McAvoy, Fassbender, Lawrence, Hoult, Till, and Peters reprise their roles in ''[[X-Men: Apocalypse]]'' (2016), where [[Sophie Turner]], [[Tye Sheridan]], [[Kodi Smit-McPhee]], and [[Alexandra Shipp]] portray younger versions of Grey, Scott Summers, [[Nightcrawler (character)|Kurt Wagner / Nightcrawler]], and Munroe. Except for Till, all new actors return in ''[[Dark Phoenix (film)|Dark Phoenix]]'' (2019).

[[Ryan Reynolds]] portrays [[Wade Wilson (film character)|Wade Wilson]] in ''X-Men Origins: Wolverine'' before starring as a new version of the character in the titular role in ''[[Deadpool (film)|Deadpool]]'' (2016), which also features a new version of Colossus played by [[Stefan Kapičić]], replacing Cudmore. Reynolds reprises his role in the short film ''[[No Good Deed (2017 film)|No Good Deed]]'' (2017), and in ''[[Deadpool 2]]'' (2018), in which Kapičić also reprises his role. [[Maisie Williams]], [[Anya Taylor-Joy]], [[Charlie Heaton]], [[Blu Hunt]], and [[Henry Zaga]] star as the [[New Mutants|titular team]] members [[Wolfsbane (character)|Rahne Sinclair]], [[Magik|Illyana Rasputin]], [[Cannonball (Marvel Comics)|Samuel Guthrie]], [[Danielle Moonstar]], and [[Sunspot (Marvel Comics)|Roberto da Costa]] in ''[[The New Mutants (film)|The New Mutants]]'' (2020).

Reynolds, Jackman, Kapičić, [[Morena Baccarin]], [[Rob Delaney]], [[Brianna Hildebrand]], [[Dafne Keen]], [[Shioli Kutsuna]], [[Tyler Mane]], [[Karan Soni]], [[Aaron Stanford]], [[Lewis Tan]], and [[Leslie Uggams]] reprise their respective roles in the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] (MCU) [[media franchise]]; the film ''[[Deadpool & Wolverine]]'' (2024) serves as a sequel to the ''Deadpool'' films.

