On February 15, 2018, Garcia was arrested for discharging a weapon in an inhabited place.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.complex.com/music/2018/02/lil-pump-arrested-for-firing-weapon|title=Lil Pump Arrested for Firing Weapon at Home|website=Complex|date=February 2018|access-date=February 15, 2018|archive-date=April 15, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190415171800/https://www.complex.com/music/2018/02/lil-pump-arrested-for-firing-weapon|url-status=live}}</ref> According to his manager, three men attempted to break into his home in San Fernando Valley at around 4 pm before shooting into the door. Police found the bullet may have come from inside the home, coming back later with a search warrant before finding an unloaded handgun below the balcony with ammunition elsewhere in the residence.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/98212-lil-pump-reportedly-arrested-for-firing-gun-in-his-home-news|title=Lil Pump Reportedly Arrested For Firing Gun In His Home|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=February 15, 2018|archive-date=March 31, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190331032845/https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/lil-pump-reportedly-arrested-for-firing-gun-in-his-home-news.43898.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Garcia's mother was subsequently investigated for endangering a minor and having an unsecured firearm at the home.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://uproxx.com/hiphop/lil-pump-arrested-for-shooting-gun-in-his-home/|title=Lil Pump Has Been Arrested For Firing A Gun Inside His Home|date=February 15, 2018|work=UPROXX|access-date=February 15, 2018|archive-date=March 31, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190331032845/https://uproxx.com/hiphop/lil-pump-arrested-for-shooting-gun-in-his-home/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On August 29, 2018, Garcia was arrested for driving without a license in Miami.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.local10.com/news/local/miami/rapper-lil-pump-arrested-for-driving-without-licence-miami-police-say|title=Rapper Lil Pump arrested for driving without license, Miami...|last=Swift|first=Tim|website=www.local10.com|access-date=September 4, 2018|date=August 30, 2018|archive-date=August 31, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180831071950/https://www.local10.com/news/local/miami/rapper-lil-pump-arrested-for-driving-without-licence-miami-police-say|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.complex.com/music/2018/08/lil-pump-lawyer-says-rappers-arrest-was-due-to-profiling|title=Lil Pump's Lawyer Says the Rapper's Arrest Was Due to Racial Profiling|website=Complex|access-date=August 31, 2018|archive-date=September 1, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180901012558/https://www.complex.com/music/2018/08/lil-pump-lawyer-says-rappers-arrest-was-due-to-profiling|url-status=live}}</ref>
On September 3, he announced that he would be going to jail for "a few months" for a parole violation stemming from the arrest.<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/lil-pump-tells-fans-hes-going-to-jail-for-a-couple-months-after-8473297/|title=Lil Pump Tells Fans He's Going to Jail for a 'Couple Months' After Violating Probation: Watch|magazine=Billboard|access-date=September 4, 2018|archive-date=September 4, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180904115935/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/hip-hop/8473297/lil-pump-tells-fans-hes-going-to-jail-for-a-couple-months-after|url-status=live}}</ref> However, he appeared on the live American television show ''[[Saturday Night Live]]'' on September 29.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2018/09/lil-pumps-saturday-night-live-performance-proves-hes-not-in-jail/|title=Lil Pump's 'SNL' Performance Proves He's Not in Jail – XXL|work=XXL Mag|access-date=September 30, 2018|archive-date=March 5, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190305221059/http://www.xxlmag.com/news/2018/09/lil-pumps-saturday-night-live-performance-proves-hes-not-in-jail/|url-status=live}}</ref> Garcia's manager told [[Billboard (magazine)|''Billboard'']] in October 2018 that Garcia had served a prison sentence, but did not give any further details.<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Lockett |first1=Dee |title=21 Under 21: Lil Pump on Recording 'I Love It' With Kanye West and Breaking Through the SoundCloud Noise |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/grammys/8479042/lil-pump-kanye-west-21-under-21-interview |access-date=October 12, 2018 |magazine=Billboard |date=October 10, 2018 |archive-date=June 29, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190629131348/https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/grammys/8479042/lil-pump-kanye-west-21-under-21-interview |url-status=live }}</ref>

On December 4, 2018, Garcia was arrested by Danish police after a performance in [[Vega, Copenhagen]], for possessing marijuana; he was fined $700–800.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.tmz.com/2018/12/05/lil-pump-released-denmark-police-weed-fine/|title=Lil Pump Released from Custody in Denmark After Paying Fine for Marijuana|website=TMZ|language=en|access-date=May 31, 2019|archive-date=May 31, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190531182826/https://www.tmz.com/2018/12/05/lil-pump-released-denmark-police-weed-fine/|url-status=live}}</ref> He later live streamed himself flipping his middle finger at a police officer while being detained. He was subsequently banned from entering the country for two years.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://ekstrabladet.dk/flash/udlandkendte/politiet-bekraefter-international-stjerne-udvist-af-danmark/7427356 |title=Politiet bekræfter: International stjerne udvist af Danmark |last1=Jespersen |first1=Linette |last2=Hellensberg |first2=Laura |website=[[Ekstra Bladet]] |date=December 6, 2018 |language=da |access-date=December 7, 2018 |archive-date=November 1, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201101064545/https://ekstrabladet.dk/flash/udlandkendte/politiet-bekraefter-international-stjerne-udvist-af-danmark/7427356 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.stereogum.com/2024938/lil-pump-detained-taunting-danish-cops-show-cancelled/news/|title=Lil Pump Detained For Taunting Danish Cops, Show Cancelled|date=December 4, 2018|website=Stereogum|access-date=May 31, 2019|archive-date=May 31, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190531182821/https://www.stereogum.com/2024938/lil-pump-detained-taunting-danish-cops-show-cancelled/news/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On December 13, 2018, Garcia was arrested at a Miami airport for [[disorderly conduct]] as he was about to take off on a flight; security wanted to search Garcia's luggage for cannabis but Garcia insisted he did not have any. While no drugs were found, during the encounter with police Garcia became angry and began arguing loudly with the security employees. He was subsequently taken into custody.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://consequence.net/2018/12/lil-pump-arrest-disorderly-conduct/|title=Lil Pump arrested for disorderly conduct after being accused of bringing drugs on airplane|date=December 14, 2018|website=Consequence of Sound|access-date=December 18, 2018|archive-date=January 17, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230117211009/https://consequence.net/2018/12/lil-pump-arrest-disorderly-conduct/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In November 2021, the [[IRS]] filed a lien on his Miami home for unpaid taxes in the amount of $1.6 million.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.complex.com/music/lil-pump-reportedly-owes-irs-over-1-million-dollars-unpaid-taxes|title=Lil Pump Reportedly Owes the IRS $1.6 Million in Unpaid Taxes|first1=Joshua|last1=Espinoza|publisher=[[Complex Networks]]|date=November 19, 2021|access-date=December 17, 2021|archive-date=December 16, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211216220746/https://www.complex.com/music/lil-pump-reportedly-owes-irs-over-1-million-dollars-unpaid-taxes|url-status=live}}</ref>

